    "content": "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>UD Outer-Face Gate Closure v0.1</title>\n<style>body{font:17px/1.6 system-ui;max-width:920px;margin:48px auto;padding:0 24px;color:#192c3e}h1,h2{line-height:1.2}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{border:1px solid #ccd5df;padding:10px;text-align:left}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;background:#eef3f7;padding:16px}</style>\n<h1>UD Outer-Face Gate Closure v0.1</h1><p>9 October 2026. Development lane; constructor-verified; physical promotion 0.</p>\n<p><strong>Result:</strong> switching the outer face 013–cell 0123 coupling breaks the previous six-coordinate record. Ten coordinates are necessary and sufficient for a common autonomous linear record retaining the original observables under this gate and independently switched shared-face couplings. Fourteen suffice, and are minimal in the same sense, when all eight face–cell incidences are independently gated.</p>\n<table><tr><th>Gate family</th><th>Exact row-closure ranks from prior six</th><th>Final dimension</th></tr><tr><td>Outer 013–0123 only</td><td>6 → 7 → 8 → 9 → 10</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>Two shared-face links and outer 013–0123</td><td>6 → 7 → 8 → 9 → 10</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>All eight face–cell links</td><td>6 → 10 → 14</td><td>14</td></tr></table>\n<h2>Fixed assumptions</h2><p>Same 23-coordinate real register on &lt;0123,0124&gt;, increasing simplex orientations, unit metric, A=Bᵀ−B. Each candidate gate multiplies both antisymmetric entries of one face–cell coupling by a real parameter. Binary values mean off/on. The original boundary and topology remain fixed; gated coefficients are dynamical controls, not replacement chain maps. All lower-degree incidence couplings remain unchanged. No physical gate-eligibility or timing law is supplied.</p>\n<h2>Counterexample</h2><pre>x+ = e0123+e013+e023\nx− = e0123−e013−e023.</pre><p>Both have the prior record (q1,q2,p1,p2,f,r)=(1,0,0,0,0,0) and full squared norm 3. With all couplings open, their retained derivatives agree. Close only the outer 013–0123 link: q1′ becomes −1 and +1 respectively. Consequently the cell stock derivatives are −2 and +2. The omitted distinction between c013 and c023 now matters because their cancellation in p1 no longer survives the gate.</p>\n<h2>Why the minimum is exact</h2><p>For each gate family, repeatedly append O A and O Li to the current readout row space O, where Li is each controlled skew incidence rotation. Stabilization gives the least common invariant row space containing the six-coordinate readout. Any common exact autonomous linear representation of that readout, valid for arbitrary real initial states and every gate setting, must contain all these rows. The saved matrices verify O A=HA O and O Li=Hi O exactly with rational arithmetic.</p>\n<p>The model has the full affine control form A+Σ(gi−1)Li; closure under A and every Li proves closure for all real gate parameters. It also proves preservation under chronological products for prescribed locally finite piecewise-constant switching. A held gate mode and decision schedule must still be supplied or represented. State-dependent eligibility must factor through the record; arbitrary reset maps require a separate test. These claims do not establish a minimum for nonlinear encodings, restricted initial states, or a single special schedule.</p>\n<h2>What the fourteen coordinates mean</h2><p>The common space can be represented by all seven face amplitudes, both cell amplitudes, and five independent edge circulations. The seven oriented face-boundary circulations have rank five. This yields 7+2+5=14 and no vertex coordinates are needed for these outputs under this particular gate family. Nine dimensions of the original register remain unobserved by these outputs for these dynamics. They have not been declared physically absent.</p>\n<p>The ten-coordinate record contains the individual outer-face amplitude c013 and both cell amplitudes. Thus a proposed eligibility predicate based on c013 q1 can be evaluated from it. The fourteen-coordinate record similarly supplies every face–cell product and gated face–cell support current. It does not guarantee eligibility closure for rules reading individual omitted edges, vertices, or external information.</p>\n<h2>Implication</h2><p>There is no universal six-coordinate compression. The sufficient record depends jointly on the desired observables and the permitted interaction family. Adding controllable interactions can activate distinctions hidden by the original reduction. Here the required state grows from 6 to 10 to 14, while remaining below 23. Coordinate reduction does not by itself prove a speedup, sparse deltas, physical admissibility, or scalable savings.</p>\n<h2>Evidence and replay</h2><p>Run <code>python verify_outer.py</code>. Standard-library Fraction arithmetic; no numerical fit or sampled integration. The output contains exact common-basis matrices, reduced generators, rank sequences, and the counterexample. Earlier baseline and shared-gate checks are rerun and packaged unchanged. Checks are constructor-written, not independent reproduction. Prior source context remains the supplied historical ledger and governance proposal; this is not a refreshed statement of the live repository.</p>\n<p><strong>Next trajectory:</strong> add lower-degree edge–face gates and determine whether the 14-dimensional reduction persists or requires more of the register. This tests where interaction freedom exhausts the available compression. The missing Gap2_FINAL_Finite_Genesis.png was not used.</p></html>\n"
