    "content": "# UD primitive-update audit and static K4 null v0.1\n\n**10 October 2026 UTC · development / constructor check · physical promotion 0.**\n\n## 1. Source boundary and object types\n\n`UD_EDGE_CLOSURE_AND_TRANSPORT_INTEGRITY_HARD_GATE_DERIVATION_v0.1.md` (21 August 2026, §§II–IV; Library `libfile_e9d5b0d7a4bc81918822ae403d527626`) defines the edge closure factor from its context-dependent required receipts and tests local lawful transport against declared domain, overlap and reverse conditions. The gate is the product \\(h_e=C_eT_e\\); nontrivial holonomy is not automatically a failure. In the contractive specialization of `UD_JOP_WORKING_MANUSCRIPT_THROUGH_SECTION11_v1.2_JOINT_REPLAY_GOVERNED.md` (30 August 2026, §§6.1–6.2, §7 v0.4; Library `libfile_8b9461fba6248191bb6d58dcf977a977`), \\(C_{{\\rm cl},e}=1-\\theta_{p(e)}\\) is a **defined context-specific lift**, while \\(T_e=\\mathbf1[I-U_e^\\dagger U_e=0]\\) is a separately typed edge-map test. Neither source supplies a primitive pre-event law that updates closure receipts or the local edge map \\(U_e\\) from native amplitude. `UD_HARD_GATE_UPDATE_LAW_SOURCE_DERIVATION_v0.1.md` (23 August 2026; Library `libfile_a80bf50559c88191a8b3b411cb38d93c`) and `HARD_GATE_TRANSITION_TRIGGER_AND_SOFT_MARGIN_SOURCE_AUDIT_v0.1.md` (28 August 2026; Library `libfile_92f3e465e4008191a62746ef92d52a4c`) leave the predicate trigger source-blocked. The supplied repository ZIP `05-DistinctionDynamics_Full_Repository_v1.zip`, `03_transport/transport_evolution_operator.md` and `02_geometry/hyperclosure_simplex_candidate.md`, contains placeholders, not a replacement law.\n\n**DERIVED necessity (fixed declared context):** If the required-receipt set, every constituent binary closure receipt, and the lawful/failure status of each typed \\(U_e\\) remain fixed, then \\(C_e,T_e,h_e\\) remain fixed. Thus an edge-mask transition requires a constituent closure-receipt change, a change in a declared requirement set, or a change in the applicable local transport test/status. This necessity supplies no event trigger or rate. The historical §7 conditional pair selector can choose a pair once its assumptions and receipts are supplied, but its pair-level \\(\\theta\\) is not a primitive local \\(U_e\\) update.\n\n## 2. Exact adversarial control\n\nState space: real oriented K4 cochains \\(C_0\\oplus C_1\\oplus C_2\\oplus C_3\\), with vertex order 0–3, edge order (01,02,03,12,13,23), face order (012,013,023,123), Euclidean cochain metric and incidence \\(B_1,B_2\\) encoded in `verify.py`. This is the native ungated skew Hodge–Dirac vertex-edge sector of the v0.39 coefficient ledger Q169 (`20-UD_COEFFICIENT_PROVENANCE_LEDGER_v0.39-2-.md`, supplied file SHA-256 `1281aa8454013fbbdbcf8ada07af0aefe81014003f25a27f3929ad43afffae63`). Dimensionless native parameter \\(s\\); no physical clock. Set \\(v=(1,-1,0,0)\\), \\(g=B_1^Tv=(-2,-1,-1,1,1,0)\\). Then \\(B_1g=4v\\), \\(B_2^Tg=0\\), and\n\n\\[\nc_0(s)=v\\cos(2s),\\quad c_1(s)=\\tfrac12g\\sin(2s),\\quad c_2(s)=c_3(s)=0.\n\\]\n\nThis solves \\(c_0'=-B_1c_1\\), \\(c_1'=B_1^Tc_0-B_2c_2\\), with zero face/cell derivatives; \\(B_1B_2=0\\). Initial condition at \\(s=0\\): \\((c_0,c_1,c_2,c_3)=(v,0,0,0)\\). Take the finite interval \\([\\pi/4,\\pi/2]\\). Opposite-edge pairs \\(A=(01,23),B=(02,13),C=(03,12)\\) have source-stock receipts \\(\\|P_pc_1\\|^2\\) from \\((1,1/2,1/2)\\) to \\((0,0,0)\\), so the historical §7 v0.4 integral signed source is exactly \\(G=(-1,-1/2,-1/2)\\), sum \\(-2\\). Zero face cochain gives burden weights zero. An **unqualified** extension of the v0.4 sign rule to any such trajectory, given initial \\(\\theta=(0,0,0)\\) and pair integrity all one, requests closure of pair A (unique largest loss).\n\nKeep the primitive structure fixed for the whole trajectory: fully retained K4 required closure receipts all one, local edge maps \\(U_e=I\\) on their declared one-dimensional complex transport spaces, and no change to requirements. Consequently