    "content": "# UD target-blind event-history eligibility audit v0.1\n\n**10 October 2026 UTC · retrospective source qualification · physical promotion 0.**\n\n## Decision and source versions\n\nThe recovered `UD_GENERATED_HISTORY_v0.1_RELEASE.zip` (Library `libfile_133d326804648191bec6931ed6744b81`, SHA-256 `85d41c897e2f846387eb59c36641b796d1be44f77a246aae67025d7003d18da7`) is **INELIGIBLE** as a target-blind test of OP03 sign-to-capacity polarity. Its `UD_GENERATED_HISTORY_PERSISTENCE_AUDIT_v0.1.md`, “Replay contract” and “Bounded results,” explicitly identifies the conditional selector as the source of switch outcomes. Its `verify_generated_history_v0_1.py` calls `select(state,theta,history=selected)`, stores its returned `after` as `theta_after`, and propagates that result. The label is therefore generated by the rule being exercised, not independently read. The 2,052 runs and 65,664 steps remain useful for their declared source-free paired-gate reachability and persistence questions.\n\nThe `UD_PAIR_SOURCE_SYNTHETIC_FIXTURE_v0.3.json` (Library `libfile_91a4bd9965d88191a4a432462f2d41e7`) explicitly labels itself a synthetic unit fixture. `UD_PAIR_SOURCE_BRIDGE_INDEPENDENT_REPRO_AUDIT_v0.1.json` (30 August 2026; Library `libfile_cf748d4887e481919d264a19804a21fb`) rules its held-out predictive replay `BLOCKED_NO_SOURCE_EVENT_HISTORY`. The related `UD_PAIR_SOURCE_EVENT_REPLAY_SCHEMA_v0.3.json` (Library `libfile_72ecb47fe1308191b77f0f6006101b69`) describes a record format; it supplies no observed event target. The two byte-identical `UD_HARD_GATE_AND_E2_FULL_DRY_RUN_v0.1.zip` archives (Library `libfile_cbb76ac8e4b08191af10dd6e5fa6ec05` and `libfile_c0ef1b2f2a708191a3c529dbb6b05b76`, SHA-256 `4edeee8738e58b0a03306075b0df3f499a58029c4b418233d5e155c0012d4509`) contain a synthetic apparatus dry run and hard-face-gate calculations, not independently produced OP03 pair-switch labels.\n\n## Exact polarity criterion\n\n`UD_MINIMAL_CAPACITY_ALIGNMENT_AXIOM_UNIQUENESS_v0.1.md` (Library `libfile_0a0f249fa2488191b7154a8d64163e09`, “Theorem” and “No-go corollary”) proves that null response, reversal covariance, and minimal one-pair response leave **two** maps \\(F(g)=+2g\\) or \\(F(g)=-2g\\), for \\(g=\\operatorname{sgn}G_\\Sigma^{S\\pm}\\) and \\(F(g)=\\Delta D_{\\rm cl}\\). The attached `UD_MINIMAL_CAPACITY_ALIGNMENT_AXIOM_AUDIT_v0.9.json` confirms the exact 27→2→1 count, with the last step supplied by the unvalidated constitutive alignment axiom. Since \\(D_{\\rm cl}=6-2w_H(\\theta)\\), an independent nonzero-\\(g\\), one-pair event with a separately read \\(\\Delta w_H=\\pm1\\) can discriminate polarity. A fixed-Hamming swap has \\(\\Delta D_{\\rm cl}=0\\), and cannot discriminate the two nonzero sign maps.\n\nThe recovered generated-history archive reports 12,171 swaps under a fixed-Hamming-one design. Its six full representative traces (192 steps) all maintain \\(w_H=1\\), and no record contains \\(G_\\Sigma^{S\\pm}\\) or primitive closure/typed local-\\(U_e\\) outcomes. `audit.py` rechecks these 192 steps with exact fractions and inspects the generator's label assignment. Separately, I reran the archived generator across all 2,052 runs and 65,664 steps: its 1,330,092 exact assertions passed, and its regenerated results SHA-256 `645493a83b8e72cc042c4a95204c96ecade04ef9e23fe5e9e7df17bdc1b3f8d3` equals the archived results hash. This is same-code reproduction and an **eligibility audit**, not an OP03 prediction score or independent scientific implementation. No negative result on the conditional sign law follows.\n\n## Required independent event record\n\nFor a prospective same-carrier test, the generator or observation must supply, **before outcome exposure**, an ordered pre-event \\(K4/\\Theta\\) state, dimensionless native interval, \\(c_0,c_1,c_2\\) or already auditable signed \\(G_p^{S\\pm}\\), pair integrity, burden lane, eligibility and prior-event boundary. The post-event \\(\\theta\\) or primitive closure/transport receipts must be produced by an independently specified process or measurement whose code does not call the candidate sign or address selector. Record the full no-event exposure windows as well as switches. For six-edge claims also supply typed local edge-map \\(U_e\\) and closure requirement/receipt states; \\(C_1\\) relative frame is a different operator.\n\nFreeze generator version/hash, state domain, timing, exclusions, baselines, predicted branch (aligned and anti-aligned), and acceptance rule before revealing independent outcomes. The primary discriminating stratum is nonzero signed source with one-pair \\(\\Delta w_H\\ne0\\); fixed-Hamming swaps and structural nulls are separately reported controls. A synthetic independent mechanism may only test mathematical model compatibility within its stated assumptions, not establish physical correspondence. The prior `source_rule_gate_v01/PROTOCOL.json` v0.1 and `UD_PAIR_SOURCE_EVENT_REPLAY_SCHEMA_v0.3.json` remain useful constraints; no after-target change to their frozen thresholds is made here.\n\n**Governance:** Retrospective qualification; no new theorem about the conditional selector, no held-out score, no AUTO_LOCK of polarity, non-constructor review pending under supplied `UD_GOVERNANCE_CRL2_SUBDIVISION_v1.0.md` §1, physical promotion 0. Source files remain immutable; this audit is an append-only development record.\n"
