    "size_bytes": 6293,
    "content": "# UD OP03 independent event intake v0.1\n\n**10 October 2026 UTC · source-blocked acquisition tool · physical promotion 0.**\n\n## Result\n\nThe three August 23 hard-gate sources were checked: `UD_HARD_GATE_PREDICATE_HISTORY_SOURCE_ADDENDUM_v0.1.md` (Library `libfile_18f257eaf4bc8191b4a5d14cc74cfe13`), `UD_HARD_GATE_MASK_TRANSITION_RECEIPT_SOURCE_ADDENDUM_v0.1.md` (`libfile_c1bc2fa815d08191956c8eaf843da431`), and `UD_HARD_GATE_MASK_HISTORY_AND_LOSS_EVENT_COUNT_AUDIT_v0.1.md` (`libfile_10e96b19567081919e4526a73d05fbb4`). They admit pre/post predicate and cause-tag **receipt bookkeeping**, but explicitly supply no transition recurrence. These face-gate receipts are not interchangeable with K4 opposite-pair \\(\\Theta\\) outcomes. `UD_MINIMAL_CAPACITY_ALIGNMENT_AXIOM_UNIQUENESS_v0.1.md` (Library `libfile_0a0f249fa2488191b7154a8d64163e09`, Theorem/No-go corollary) leaves two conditional polarity maps \\(F_\\pm(g)=\\pm2g\\), where \\(g=\\operatorname{sgn}\\sum_pG_p^{S\\pm}\\) and \\(F=\\Delta D_{\\rm cl}\\). No independently produced same-carrier target history was recovered. The previous [eligibility audit](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-10T165456Z-codex-event-eligibility-d4d33a75) explains why the 2,052-run generated archive cannot serve as that target.\n\nThis package provides an exact **intake and scoring instrument**, not a source law or dataset. It scores only the conditional one-pair *capacity polarity* on the K4/C1/opposite-pair/Theta carrier. It does not predict pair address, first-admissible event time, six-edge \\(U_e\\), or physical behavior. The native parameter \\(s\\) is dimensionless.\n\n## Required independent input and sequence\n\n1. An outcome producer other than the historical sign/address selector must emit ordered \\(\\Theta\\) outcomes from independently specified model code or direct same-carrier observations. Commit the producer code/measurement protocol before prediction. For an already produced sealed file, precommit its SHA-256 without exposing its labels. For a future acquisition, freeze the protocol now and hash the outcome immediately when it is acquired. A verbal independence assertion alone is insufficient; an external reviewer must inspect the producer and chronology. Do not use the historical selector to make target labels.\n2. `manifest.json` must have `schema=\"UD-OP03-POLARITY-INTAKE-v0.1\"`, `carrier=\"K4/C1/opposite-pair/Theta\"`, `source_version`, SHA-256 strings for `source_computation_sha256`, `pre_event_generator_sha256`, `eligibility_rule_sha256`; `outcome_acquisition_mode=\"precommitted_file\"` with `independent_outcome_sha256` as SHA-256, **or** `outcome_acquisition_mode=\"future_acquisition\"` with `independent_outcome_sha256=null`; `outcome_producer={\"kind\":\"independent_model\"|\"measurement\",\"artifact_sha256\":\"...\",\"independence_evidence\":\"...\"}`; `time_parameter=\"native dimensionless s\"`; and `claim_scope=\"conditional one-pair capacity polarity; no physical promotion\"`. Archive the raw source history and code corresponding to these hashes. These fields are declarations; the script checks format and available commitment consistency, not provenance truth.\n3. `pre_event.jsonl` contains **every consecutive eligible and control window**, one JSON object per line with a unique `event_id`, `s_start`, `s_end` as canonical exact rational strings, `theta_minus` and `pair_integrity` as three binary values ordered A=(01,23), B=(02,13), C=(03,12), `signed_G_by_pair` as three exact rational strings computed on the ungated source, `prior_event_boundary`, `state_receipt_sha256`, and `eligible_before_outcome` as a boolean fixed without seeing the target. The latter requires an external source-addressability rule, not an outcome-derived event subtype. Record the raw \\(c_0,c_1,c_2\\), incidence conventions and integration method in the source history so the signed \\(G\\) can be recomputed independently. No target field belongs in this file.\n4. Run `python3 intake.py prepare manifest.json pre_event.jsonl predictions.jsonl freeze.json` in an environment that cannot read the outcomes. It writes aligned, anti-aligned and zero-capacity-change baseline forecasts for all precommitted rows, and hashes the manifest, source file and predictions. The primary stratum requires nonzero signed \\(G\\), pre-outcome eligibility, both open and closed integrity-passing pairs, and \\(w_H(\\theta^-)\\in\\{1,2\\}\\). No threshold is fitted. Commit the predictions and freeze receipt before the target is made available.\n5. `outcomes.jsonl` contains one row per same ordered `event_id` with `theta_plus`, `target_receipt_sha256`, and `producer_artifact_sha256` equal to the committed producer artifact hash. Run `python3 intake.py score manifest.json pre_event.jsonl predictions.jsonl freeze.json outcomes.jsonl`. It refuses a changed manifest, source, prediction, precommitted target hash (when present), row order, or missing record. In future-acquisition mode it records the newly acquired target hash for independent custody review. It reports aligned/anti-aligned capacity-direction matches, non-events/swaps, invalid multi-pair outcomes, and a capacity-persistence baseline. A fixed-Hamming swap is a control, not a polarity discriminator.\n\n## Decision and limits\n\nThe scorer **never** emits a validated-rule or physical-promotion verdict. If no nonzero-source one-pair capacity change is observed, it reports `NO_DISCRIMINATING_EVENT`. Otherwise it reports counts pending non-constructor review. That reviewer must verify independent outcome production, prospective custody, source-window reachability, raw signed-source calculation, exclusion rule and all observed nulls before any CRL-2b/2c request. Under the attached `UD_GOVERNANCE_CRL2_SUBDIVISION_v1.0.md` §1 (a **governance proposal**, not an independently validated science result), constructor checks alone remain at 2a. One scoped event can distinguish the two exact algebraic maps; repeatability and independent physical correspondence require separate evidence. Physical promotion remains 0.\n\n**OPEN input:** a real versioned same-carrier corpus or a source-authored independent generator with its code, raw pre-event cochains, externally fixed eligibility, and post-event \\(\\Theta\\) receipts. The unavailable `Gap2_FINAL_Finite_Genesis.png` was not read or used.\n"
