    "size_bytes": 7946,
    "content": "# UD direct-Theta event to typed closure and hard-mask pushforward v0.1\n\n**10 October 2026 UTC · append-only source-scope amendment and exact conditional theorem · physical promotion 0.**\n\n## Source recovery and correction\n\n`UD_THETA_FLIP_DIRECT_EVENT_INPUT_SOURCE_ADDENDUM_v0.1.md` (26 August 2026; Library `libfile_6145629eb8c081919302d99d60df1c82`, “Transition,” “Local source protocol,” and “Missing source”) is an **admitted internal interface**. It defines\n\n\\[\n\\Theta^+=P_g\\Theta^-\\oplus\\xi,\n\\qquad \\Theta,\\xi\\in\\mathbb F_2^3,\n\\]\n\nfor a provenance-bound direct event input \\(\\xi\\) with current class `EXTERNAL_QUARANTINED`. `UD_THETA_FLIP_DIRECT_PRIMITIVE_SOURCE_ADDENDUM_AUDIT_v0.1.md` (26 August; Library `libfile_176d2121e0708191bbc529c33a92cafc`, §§II–VIII and X) proves direction/count and covariance for a **supplied** \\(\\xi\\), while explicitly leaving its endogenous cause open. The package `UD_OMEGA0_PHASE23_THETA_EVENT_AND_CONTROL_BOUNDARY_PACKAGE_v0.1.zip` (Library `libfile_5c9aeab36a448191bf27669bf18f1099`, SHA-256 `b6037a5610d19937178801de3078371b017c16b08fa0f29d78f6e2d0b25f50a0`) contains a quarantine wrapper and 384 conditional test cases. It contains no independent pre-event signed \\(G_p^{S\\pm}\\) matched to outcomes. The separate `UD_THETA_HISTORY_TO_CLOSURE_GATE_HISTORY_THEOREM_v0.1.md` (23 August; Library `libfile_bb82dc6467288191ac6691c1ef6019cf`) pushes an **already supplied** ordered \\(\\Theta\\)-history to edge closure masks.\n\n**Amendment to prior wording:** The [historical selector scope report](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-10T164302Z-codex-historical-pair-5b327476), [static-null audit](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-10T164734Z-codex-native-static-null-b71cb9e8), and [intake source audit](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-10T165944Z-codex-op03-intake-ed488bce) used “primitive update open” without enumerating this admitted exogenous direct-\\(\\Theta\\) interface. The precise result is: **post-event \\(\\Theta\\) and its closure-factor lift are exact once a valid external flip receipt is supplied; an endogenous/pre-event predictor of \\(\\xi\\) and a local edge transport-integrity update remain OPEN.** The prior artifacts remain immutable. This correction changes no physical status.\n\n## New exact typed consequence\n\nDomain: a fixed labeled K4 with opposite-edge pairs \\(A=(01,23),B=(02,13),C=(03,12)\\), pre-state \\(\\Theta^-\\in\\mathbb F_2^3\\), a sourced pair permutation \\(P_g\\), flip receipt \\(\\xi\\in\\mathbb F_2^3\\), and six independently typed binary local edge transport-integrity values \\(T_e\\). Let \\(Y=P_g\\Theta^-\\). The closure factor in this **specific pair-lift context** is \\(C_{{\\rm cl},e}=1-\\theta_{p(e)}\\); this is not a claim that all context-dependent closure requirement sets are pair-identical. Compare pre/post in the same relabeled edge frame. Then\n\n\\[\nC_{{\\rm cl},e}^-=1-Y_{p(e)},\\quad\nC_{{\\rm cl},e}^+=1-(Y_{p(e)}\\oplus\\xi_{p(e)}),\\quad\nC_{{\\rm cl},e}^-\\oplus C_{{\\rm cl},e}^+=\\xi_{p(e)}.\n\\]\n\nEach flipped pair changes **two closure factors**, so \\(C_E^{\\rm cl}=2\\sum_p(1-Y_p)\\xi_p\\) and \\(O_E^{\\rm cl}=2\\sum_pY_p\\xi_p\\). If the six \\(T_e\\) remain fixed across this update and \\(h_e=C_{{\\rm cl},e}T_e\\), the counts of actual **hard-mask** closures and openings are instead\n\n\\[\nC_E^{\\rm hard}=\\sum_p(1-Y_p)\\xi_p\\sum_{e\\in M_p}T_e,\n\\qquad\nO_E^{\\rm hard}=\\sum_pY_p\\xi_p\\sum_{e\\in M_p}T_e.\n\\]\n\nThus \\(0\\le C_E^{\\rm hard}\\le C_E^{\\rm cl}\\) and similarly for openings. The two counts agree only if the flipped relevant edge transport predicates pass. If \\(T_e\\) itself changes, use the typed post-state \\(h_e^+=C_{{\\rm cl},e}^+T_e^+\\); the fixed-\\(T\\) count theorem cannot be applied. \\(U_e\\) (the local edge map tested by \\(T_e\\)) is not the oriented global \\(C_1\\) transport used to recover a relative frame.\n\n**Proof:** The XOR identity is coordinatewise over \\(\\mathbb F_2\\); each pair has exactly two edges. A closure is \\((Y_p,\\xi_p)=(0,1)\\), an opening is \\((1,1)\\). Multiplying each changing closure bit by fixed \\(T_e\\) gives the two weighted sums. No numeric coefficient or physical metric is introduced. `verify.py` exhausts all \\(8\\) pre-states, \\(6\\) pair permutations, \\(8\\) flip masks and \\(64\\) transport masks: **24,576** exact cases and **147,456** pair-relabeling covariance comparisons. For pre-state \\((0,1,0)\\) and all \\(T_e=1\\), flip \\((1,0,0)\\) closes A while flip \\((0,1,0)\\) reopens B; both satisfy the admitted *conditional* interface. If one A-edge transport gate is already failed, the A flip changes two closure factors but only one hard-mask bit.\n\nThe Phase 23 source verifier's direct-\\(\\Theta\\) block (lines 1–43 of `verify_ud_omega0_phase23_v0_1.py`, original SHA-256 `6709d5ab6c7f98c96a15badc660e7d32ddee7845a25ca596ef2143247d8cb8a2`) was rerun against its original quarantine module (SHA-256 `49ce70c77f80dfa0bede388b4fc2f000b473ad9ab48e5268e54305a0158d512b`) with only its absolute `/mnt/data` base path rebound to the extracted package directory. It passed **384** direct-event cases, covariance, and missing-receipt deferral. The complete original verifier could not be rerun in this environment because its separate control-boundary block imports `0runtime_full_module_v0_3_payload_guard_sync.py`, absent from that package; no control verification is claimed here. `source_rerun/source_theta_only_rerun.py` preserves the path-adapted block and `source_rerun/theta_flip_event_quarantine_contract_v0_1.py` preserves the path-adapted module. The new `verify.py` independently implements the closure and fixed-\\(T\\) mask enumeration.\n\n## Endogenous source and independent-history limit\n\nThe same pre-state \\(\\Theta^-\\), pair frame and typed \\(T\\) admit distinct post-states when independent valid external \\(\\xi\\) receipts are supplied. This is an **exact formal nonidentifiability witness for deriving \\(\\xi\\) from those pre-inputs alone**, not a claim that both histories arise under one undiscovered native dynamics. It refines, rather than supersedes, the identity/complement diagnostic countermodels in `UD_PREDICTIVE_EVENT_SOURCE_CONTRACT_v0.1.md` (28 September; Library `libfile_fa387efebcf88191ac038e30927d49c7`, §3). Current sources do not define a map from the signed source \\(G_p^{S\\pm}\\), cochains, closure-defect state, or admissibility to \\(\\xi\\). The historical §7 v0.4 sign-to-capacity rule remains a conditional candidate, not the source of the admitted flip receipt.\n\nAn independently produced `EXTERNAL_QUARANTINED` \\(\\xi\\) history could be an OP03 **target** only if its provider did not call the candidate selector and the same carrier has raw pre-event cochains or auditable signed \\(G_p^{S\\pm}\\), eligibility, ordered event boundaries and independent outcomes. The Phase 23 package provides no such paired history; the September 14 `PARITY_QUOTIENT_HELD_OUT_EVENT_REPLAY_v0.1.md` (Library `libfile_b2bfd31d6dd08191939959380aac2af0`, §§2–6) labels its 1,152 cases synthetic and its empirical target source-blocked. Its parity quotient also loses even-bit endpoint differences, so it cannot replace a full \\(\\Theta\\) score. `UD_OP03_JOINT_REPLAY_RUNTIME_PATCH_v0.9.json` (Library `libfile_85a55a0fb59c8191a9c35d23cf68f71e`) explicitly marks the independent event corpus OPEN and empirical held-out status NOT_RUN. The previous [two-stage intake](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-10T165944Z-codex-op03-intake-ed488bce) remains suitable for the conditional capacity-polarity comparison once a source-authenticated independent target exists.\n\n**Governance:** Exact conditional algebra and enumeration; no AUTO_LOCK of autonomous dynamics, physical correspondence, or sign-to-capacity alignment. No held-out event scored. Non-constructor review pending. Physical promotion 0. The supplied CRL-2 subdivision v1.0 remains a governance proposal; this constructor calculation cannot promote a bridge rung.\n"
