    "content": "# UD pre-event structural eligibility boundary v0.1\n\n**10 October 2026 UTC · development — no registry entry · physical promotion 0.**\n\n## Sources, carrier, and question\n\nThe hard edge gate is \\(h_e=C_{{\\rm cl},e}T_{{\\rm int},e}\\), with context-specific required closure receipts and typed local transport-map tests (`UD_EDGE_CLOSURE_AND_TRANSPORT_INTEGRITY_HARD_GATE_DERIVATION_v0.1.md`, 21 August 2026, §§II–IV, Library `libfile_e9d5b0d7a4bc81918822ae403d527626`). The supplied coefficient ledger `UD_COEFFICIENT_PROVENANCE_LEDGER_v0.39(2).md` (local SHA-256 recorded in previous source-readiness capture; Q20 and Q156/Q167/Q169/Q173) defines \\(\\delta_p=W_p-\\frac13\\sum_qW_q\\) and records \\(\\delta=0\\) on the equal-cell star. It does not define a closure-event trigger. The `UD_THETA_FLIP_DIRECT_EVENT_INPUT_SOURCE_ADDENDUM_v0.1.md` (26 August, Library `libfile_6145629eb8c081919302d99d60df1c82`, “Transition” and “Local source protocol”) admits an external provenance-bound \\(\\xi\\) interface and leaves the endogenous source open. `UD_DIRECTED_PARITY_SOURCE_LAW_v0.1.md` (30 August, Library `libfile_390cc189307081919ee5ee881fbc0005`, §§5–8, 12) states minimal capacity alignment as a conditional constitutive choice and its first-admissible selector as conditional on source-addressable events. `UD_THETA_EXPOSURE_TRANSPORT_EXECUTION_v0.2.md` (30 August, Library `libfile_2206a18fb0748191ba407b22ef9a1488`, §§0–2, Gate B) independently identifies the pre-event toggle as not determined by current fields.\n\nQuestion: can **pre-event structural data** exclude the exact fixed-structure K4 null while providing a nontrivial positive event-ready predicate? Keep the K4 opposite-pair \\(\\Theta\\), six local edge maps \\(U_e\\), closure receipts \\(r_\\alpha\\), relative frame, signed support \\(G_p^{S\\pm}\\), burden \\(W_p^{B2}\\), and eventual \\(\\xi\\) typed separately. No physical time or unit conversion is assumed.\n\n## The sourced negative certificate\n\nLet a model declaration available **before** the attempt interval certify that the required closure sets, all their constituent binary receipts, and each declared local transport-map predicate remain constant throughout that interval. For every edge,\n\n\\[\n C_e^+=C_e^-,\\quad T_e^+=T_e^-,\\quad h_e^+=h_e^-.\n\\]\n\nThis is an **EXACT conditional veto**: the eligible set of structural hard-mask switches on that certified fixed-structure interval is empty, regardless of the ungated cochain dynamics or signed support receipts. It excludes the exact K4 trajectory in [the fixed-structure null capture](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-10T164734Z-codex-native-static-null-b71cb9e8), whose declared \\(r,U\\) are constant while \\(G=(-1,-\\tfrac12,-\\tfrac12)\\). The certificate is a constitutive model declaration, **not** a conclusion from the current values of \\(r,U,c\\); checking post-event invariance and calling it pre-event eligibility would leak the outcome. If there is no fixed-structure certificate or sourced evolution for \\(r,U\\), the safe result is `UNRESOLVED`, not `ELIGIBLE`.\n\n## Adversarial contrast candidate\n\nA tempting source-variable gate is \\(E_\\delta=\\mathbf1[\\sum_p\\delta_p^2>0]\\). It is pair-relabeling invariant and uses no fitted tolerance. It excludes the static null because \\(W=(0,0,0)\\), but it is **NO-GO as a universal UD event-ready rule** under the currently admitted direct-\\(\\Theta\\) interface: at the same zero-contrast values, that interface validates a properly formed externally provided \\(\\xi=(1,0,0)\\) receipt. This is an algebraic model-completion counterexample, not a claim that such an event is physically reachable on the fixed-structure trajectory. An extra constitutive axiom restricting external receipt eligibility could create a new branch, but is not present in the cited sources. On the ledger's equal-cell star, \\(E_\\delta\\) would veto all events, so it also cannot serve as a general genesis rule without that new assumption.\n\nThe exact finite audit `verify.py` runs all \\(8\\) \\(\\Theta\\) states, \\(8\\) pair-integrity masks, \\(27\\) signed source triples with values \\(-1,0,1\\), and \\(27\\) burden triples with values \\(0,1,2\\): **46,656 synthetic inputs**. There are **5,184** zero-contrast inputs. The historical *conditional* selector emits an event on **1,314** of those, all with nonzero total source; the contrast gate would suppress those candidate outputs. These are disagreements between conditional formulas on synthetic inputs, not scored empirical false negatives. The fixed K4 null and a separately formed zero-contrast Phase 23 receipt are explicit controls. `results.json` contains counts; no endpoint data were fitted.\n\n## Independent event acquisition\n\nThe prior [OP03 two-stage intake v0.1](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-10T165944Z-codex-op03-intake-ed488bce) already freezes an input format for ordered pre-event raw cochains or auditable signed \\(G\\), null exposure windows, eligibility fixed before outcomes, independent same-carrier post-event \\(\\Theta\\), and producer/code hashes. The known `UD_GENERATED_HISTORY_v0.1_RELEASE.zip` (Library `libfile_133d326804648191bec6931ed6744b81`) is ineligible because its post-event labels were produced by the candidate selector, as documented in [the eligibility audit](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-10T165456Z-codex-event-eligibility-d4d33a75). `UD_OP03_JOINT_REPLAY_RUNTIME_PATCH_v0.9.json` (Library `libfile_85a55a0fb59c8191a9c35d23cf68f71e`, replay.independent_event_corpus) still says OPEN and empirical held-out NOT_RUN. A Library title/content search for same-carrier histories, pre-event cochains and outcome files found no qualifying new producer. The attached `Gap2_FINAL_STATUS.md` concerns an older genesis/spectral-index simulation, not K4/\\(\\Theta\\) event receipts. `Gap2_FINAL_Finite_Genesis.png` was unavailable and was neither read nor used.\n\n**Acquisition disposition:** no independent target or new producer was obtained; no score was run. The exact missing input is a versioned same-carrier producer or dataset independent of the selector, with its code and hash, complete ordered pre-event cochains/eligibility/no-event windows, and post-event \\(\\Theta\\) receipts. Do not alter the frozen OP03 intake thresholds after seeing outcomes.\n\n## Governance result\n\n**EXACT:** fixed-structure veto and finite candidate-disagreement counts. **CANDIDATE / NO-GO under current broad interface:** nonzero burden contrast as a universal positive event-ready gate. **OPEN:** a sourced structural transition generator, positive event eligibility, independent target and physical bridge. This remains constructor development work; no AUTO_LOCK of autonomous dynamics, no claim of physical reachability for synthetic receipts, and physical promotion 0. `UD_GOVERNANCE_CRL2_SUBDIVISION_v1.0.md` (user-supplied, Library `libfile_93b66da4fd448191a2b04ca03b93e58c`, §§1–4) is a governance proposal; non-constructor review is pending.\n"
