    "content": "# UD local transport update boundary v0.1\n\n**10 October 2026 UTC · development — no registry entry · physical promotion 0.**\n\n## Question and source discipline\n\nThe user-selected task is to derive a primitive pre-event update for a closure receipt or local edge transport map, then test an independent K4/\\(\\Theta\\) event history if one exists. The source baseline is `UD_EDGE_CLOSURE_AND_TRANSPORT_INTEGRITY_HARD_GATE_DERIVATION_v0.1.md` (21 August 2026, §§II–IV; Library `libfile_e9d5b0d7a4bc81918822ae403d527626`), where \\(C_e\\) is a context-dependent conjunction of closure receipts, \\(T_e\\) checks a locally lawful typed map, and \\(h_e=C_eT_e\\). `UD_HARD_GATE_UPDATE_LAW_SOURCE_DERIVATION_v0.1.md` (23 August, §§1–5; `libfile_a80bf50559c88191a8b3b411cb38d93c`) and `UD_HARD_GATE_BOOLEAN_FACTOR_UPDATE_THEOREM_v0.1.md` (23 August, Gate closure/opening and What is not derived; `libfile_10b3069a88a48191bd7190f02f91807b`) close conditional factor logic and explicitly leave predicate dynamics source-blocked. The historical `UD_JOP_WORKING_MANUSCRIPT_THROUGH_SECTION11_v1.2_JOINT_REPLAY_GOVERNED.md` (30 August, Library `libfile_8b9461fba6248191bb6d58dcf977a977`, §6.2) specializes the local transport test to exact isometry in a contractive sector. This specialization is **not** the general typed transport condition of the August 21 source. The later `TETRAHEDRAL_PACKET_COMPLEXES_JOP_LEAN_MANUSCRIPT_v2.36_EMPIRICAL_SCORER.md` (Library `libfile_07b844f603188191bdcaccc29c065d54`, Abstract and §1) still calls event choice a constitutive open issue. The user's supplied ledger v0.39(2), Q156/Q167/Q169/Q173, specifies currents with *given* hard masks, not primitive mask dynamics.\n\nThe supplied local `master_action.md` and `seam_phase_transport.md` files are explicitly placeholder content in the reconstructed repository snapshot. They cannot supply a missing rule. The public [UD site](https://tetrahedral-packet-complexes.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/) reports physical promotion 0 and independent review pending as of this source check.\n\n## Conditional exact local map class\n\nThis is a **new candidate model class**, not a recovered UD constitutive law. Let \\(V_e\\cong\\mathbb R^d\\) have a fixed Euclidean metric and declared domain/codomain. Let the pre-event local map \\(U_n:V_e\\to V_e\\) be a contraction and the **supplied** update components be an orthogonal \\(R_n\\) and a contraction \\(K_n\\) with \\(K_n^TK_n\\preceq I\\). Define\n\n\\[\nU_{n+1}=R_nK_nU_n,\\qquad\nQ_n=I-U_n^TU_n,\\qquad T_n=\\mathbf1[Q_n=0].\n\\]\n\nThe exact algebra gives\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{Q_{n+1}-Q_n=U_n^T(I-K_n^TK_n)U_n\\succeq0.}\n\\]\n\nConsequently \\(T_n=0\\Rightarrow T_{n+1}=0\\), because a nonzero positive semidefinite \\(Q_n\\) cannot decrease to zero. If \\(T_n=1\\), square \\(U_n\\) is invertible and\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{T_{n+1}=\\mathbf1[K_n^TK_n=I].}\n\\]\n\nThis is an **EXACT conditional pre-step transition rule once \\(K_n,R_n\\) are supplied before the event**. It is covariant under consistent orthogonal changes of basis. If the proposed \\(K_n\\) is a self-loss function with \\(K(Q=0,c)^TK(Q=0,c)=I\\) for every admitted cochain state \\(c\\), the clean set \\(Q=0\\) is invariant under this discrete rule: it cannot spontaneously create a transport-integrity failure. To trigger one from a clean state requires a sourced **transverse nonisometric step** or a different primitive event mechanism. A pure contractive composition can never reopen exact hard transport integrity; reopening needs a reset/repreparation, changed fiber/metric, or a map class outside these assumptions. This says nothing about a distinct pair-level \\(\\Theta\\) closure/reopening.\n\nThe same type discipline makes the gap explicit: neither \\(K_n\\) nor \\(R_n\\) is derived from the pre-event UD chain cochains, defect field, closure receipts, or admissibility. Passing them as named inputs is a conditional model, not a native predictor. Choosing \\(K_n\\prec I\\) whenever \\(G_\\Sigma<0\\) would fail the [fixed-structure K4 null](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-10T164734Z-codex-native-static-null-b71cb9e8), which has negative signed source while its declared local maps stay isometric. Assigning a post-event \\(K_n\\) after seeing the switch would leak the target.\n\n## Finite exact check and countermodels\n\n`verify.py` uses rational \\(2\\times2\\) maps, eight signed permutation isometries and nine diagonal contractions with singular values in \\(\\{0,\\tfrac12,1\\}\\). It checks all **5,184** two-step paths from \\(U_0=I\\), including **2,880** paths with first-step rank loss. The exact Gram increment is positive semidefinite in every case and **zero reopenings** occur; the counts are enumerations, not probabilities. An isometric nonidentity signed permutation leaves \\(T=1\\); the source-loss-to-contraction shortcut gives a false trigger on the fixed K4 null. The general statements follow from the displayed algebra, not the finite cases alone.\n\nTwo different pre-event completions with identical \\((c_n,U_n)\\) remain lawful in this declared model: \\(K_n=I\\) preserves integrity; \\(K_n=\\operatorname{diag}(\\tfrac12,1)\\) fails it. Thus the new model class exposes the exact missing input instead of deriving its value. The map class is intentionally narrow; the broad August 21 typed transport test may allow other behavior.\n\n## Independent target acquisition status\n\nThe frozen `UD_OP03_INDEPENDENT_EVENT_ACQUISITION_PROTOCOL_v0.1.md` (30 August; Library `libfile_30fb9c2688f08191acb9119bfdb6a2f4`) requires pre-event oriented cochains/transport, signed support and burden receipts, integrity and event boundary, predictor hash and time of target access, then sealed endpoint frame and \\(\\Theta\\) outcome. The [OP03 two-stage intake](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-10T165944Z-codex-op03-intake-ed488bce) supplies a specific scorer. The known `UD_GENERATED_HISTORY_v0.1_RELEASE.zip` (Library `libfile_133d326804648191bec6931ed6744b81`) is ineligible: its outcomes call the candidate selector, as proved in the [eligibility audit](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-10T165456Z-codex-event-eligibility-d4d33a75). `UD_FINITE_ADMISSION_FEEDBACK_AUDIT_v0.1.md` (2 October; `libfile_60c09498a2208191a896154f1c9fe8d8`) studies local crossings and finite slots on a distinct two-tetrahedron amplitude carrier; its synthetic traces are not independent K4/\\(\\Theta\\) event endpoints. A fresh Library search after the previous capture found only new MQM-specific files, no qualifying OP03 target. `Gap2_FINAL_Finite_Genesis.png` was unavailable and was not inspected.\n\n**NO_DATA / NOT_RUN:** no independent same-carrier history or newly authenticated event producer was acquired, so no OP03 held-out score was attempted. The exact missing input remains a versioned independent producer/dataset with ordered raw pre-event cochains, null windows, frozen eligibility, source code/hash, and sealed post-event \\(\\Theta\\) receipts. This status is an acquisition finding, not a negative empirical result.\n\n## Disposition\n\n**EXACT CONDITIONAL:** the contraction-class Gram recurrence and one-way integrity theorem. **NO-GO, scoped:** pure contraction cannot reopen the isometry hard gate; smooth self-loss that is isometric at \\(Q=0\\) cannot trigger its first failure. **OPEN:** a source-derived transverse \\(K_n\\) or closure-receipt generator, a sourced event schedule, and independent OP03 target. No autonomous dynamics is AUTO_LOCKed; the constructor check is development work. The user's `UD_GOVERNANCE_CRL2_SUBDIVISION_v1.0.md` (Library `libfile_93b66da4fd448191a2b04ca03b93e58c`, §§1–4) is a governance proposal; non-constructor review pending. Physical promotion 0.\n"
