    "content": "# UD connected seam connection and discrete-event boundary v0.1\n\n**11 October 2026 UTC · development — no registry entry · physical promotion 0.**\n\n## Question and source identities\n\nCan pre-event UD phase/connection data produce a typed local transport update and decide a hard-mask or K4/`Theta` event? The 21 August `UD_EDGE_CLOSURE_AND_TRANSPORT_INTEGRITY_HARD_GATE_DERIVATION_v0.1.md`, §§I–IV (Library `libfile_e9d5b0d7a4bc81918822ae403d527626`), separates closure from holonomy and defines `h_e=C_eT_e` using required closure receipts and a lawful local transport predicate. The 30 August `UD_JOP_WORKING_MANUSCRIPT_THROUGH_SECTION11_v1.2_JOINT_REPLAY_GOVERNED.md`, §6.2 (`libfile_8b9461fba6248191bb6d58dcf977a977`), has an exact-isometry transport specialization `T_e=1[I-U_e^*U_e=0]`. The supplied `UD_COEFFICIENT_PROVENANCE_LEDGER_v0.39(2).md`, Q156/Q167/Q169/Q173, uses given hard masks with native support operators; it does not generate a seam update.\n\n`UD_COFACE_NEWBORN_PACKET_TRANSPORT_INHERITANCE_AND_FORMATION_DEBIT_RECEIPT_TESTBED_v0.1.md` (3 October; Library `libfile_1ec04cb5aeb88191bfbe754c85d327ca`, §§1–5) exhibits a continuous seam family after structural closure, with two common-axis gauge-invariant newborn differences. It therefore supplies a source-owned **underdetermination control**: closure and inherited face transports do not choose a new seam. `UD_THETA_TRANSPORT_LIFT_v0.1.md` (30 August; `libfile_baae91f0c9d081918c739c6524668e9d`, §§2, 4, 6, 11–12) constructs a distinct eight-dimensional `Theta` representation and explicitly leaves the packet-transport-to-`S_3` receipt and pre-event parity selector open. Its affine receipt `a_e=theta_e^+ XOR P_sigma theta_e^-` is reconstructed from the endpoint; it cannot be used as a pre-event predictor.\n\n## Typed connected testbed\n\nFix a labeled, fully retained filled K4 with Euclidean one-complex-dimensional node fibers `V_i=C` and pre-event oriented links `u_{ij}:V_i→V_j` of modulus one. Set `u_{ji}=u_{ij}^{-1}` and allow gauge changes `u_{ij}→g_j u_{ij}g_i^{-1}`, `g_i∈U(1)`. This is a **declared common-axis candidate sector** of a packet seam connection, not a derivation that identifies the general UD internal edge transport with phase. All required closure receipts are one. The candidate state space `X=U(1)^6` is connected. A conditional phase evolution would be `u_{ij,n+1}=exp(i alpha_{ij,n})u_{ij,n}`, with real pre-event one-cochain `alpha_n`, initial link values and fixed boundary context; UD has not supplied a constitutive `alpha_n`.\n\nOn this candidate sector, each `u_{ij}` is unitary and has a well-typed inverse, so **under the §6.2 exact-isometry specialization** `Q_{T,ij}=I-u_{ij}^*u_{ij}=0`, `T_{ij}=1`, and `h_{ij}=1` for every phase update. Holonomy around `ijk` is `u_{ki}u_{jk}u_{ij}` and may differ from the identity without integrity failure. This is a lawful testbed under its declared full node domains; it does not assert that every possible UD context has the same transport conditions. The identity links reproduce the [frozen K4 static-null completion v0.1](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-10T164734Z-codex-native-static-null-b71cb9e8), including its fixed mask despite `G=(-1,-1/2,-1/2)`. Nonzero support loss does not change that conclusion.\n\n## Exact finite census and topological obstruction\n\n`verify.py` takes the exact fourth-root subgroup `mu_4={1,i,-1,-i}` for each of six edges. Of `4^6=4096` exact assignments, `4^3=64` are flat; each is a pure gauge assignment after fixing one vertex phase. The remaining `4032` are nonflat and **all** pass the exact-isometry integrity test. There are `64` holonomy/gauge classes in this finite grid. These are counts of phase assignments, not event probabilities, and are not a sampled continuum result. The code also rechecks all `8×6=48` affine `Theta` permutation lifts on their **separate** eight-state carrier; each is unitary, and some change Hamming weight. Their unitarity does not identify them with the one-dimensional edge links.\n\n**EXACT topological theorem (declared assumptions).** Let `D` be `Theta=F_2^3` or the finite matching-frame group `S_3` with the discrete topology. Any continuous selector `F:X→D` on connected `X=U(1)^6` is constant: its image is connected in a discrete set and thus contains one point. If normalized at identity to `000` or the identity frame, it takes that value everywhere. The same proof holds on any connected component of a continuous Spin(3)/SO(2) seam sector, with fixed discrete structural receipts. No group-homomorphism assumption is needed.\n\n**NO-GO, scoped:** continuous phase motion alone, read through a globally continuous map with fixed labeled structure, cannot select a nontrivial discrete `Theta` toggle or matching-frame permutation. Separately, isometric phase motion cannot cause a `T_e` failure under the exact-isometry specialization. This does **not** prohibit a sourced discontinuity, singularity, topology-changing admission, discrete receipt, threshold with fixed boundary rule, or nonunitary retained-environment channel. It specifies what extra input must be sourced and frozen before claims of occurrence or timing.\n\nThe candidate [native-flow projection boundary v0.1](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-11T010749Z-codex-native-projection-c9c95ae7) used `P_e exp(sA)P_e` on a **chain edge subspace** and produced a transient Gram defect. That compression and this unitary **internal seam fiber** are different carriers and maps; neither can be silently substituted for the other.\n\n## Independent K4/`Theta` producer search\n\nThe frozen `UD_OP03_INDEPENDENT_EVENT_ACQUISITION_PROTOCOL_v0.1.md` (30 August; Library `libfile_30fb9c2688f08191acb9119bfdb6a2f4`) and [two-stage intake v0.1](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-10T165944Z-codex-op03-intake-ed488bce) require an independent producer, ordered raw pre-event cochains/transport and null windows, a frozen prediction hash, and sealed post-event `Theta` receipts. The full Library title/content search for independent event histories and the GitHub code search for `pre_event.jsonl`/`outcomes.jsonl` found no qualifying same-carrier producer. A newly retrieved `PRE_EVENT_HELDOUT_PROTOCOL_v0.1.md` (Library `libfile_45b13c3166b481919c5085094719845f`) is a **protocol**, not a target corpus. The known generated-history archive is ineligible because the historical candidate selector makes its labels ([eligibility audit](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-10T165456Z-codex-event-eligibility-d4d33a75)). The unavailable `Gap2_FINAL_Finite_Genesis.png` was not inspected.\n\n**NO_DATA / NOT_RUN:** no independent OP03 score was run. The exact missing input is a versioned independent producer or observations with source code/hash and custody chronology, consecutive admissible and null windows, raw pre-event state, fixed eligibility, and separately sealed post-event `Theta` outcomes. Searches do not prove nonexistence outside the inspected sources. Repeating a candidate-built simulation cannot fill this gate.\n\n## Disposition\n\n**EXACT conditional:** the typed unitary connection census and connected-to-discrete theorem. **NO-GO, scoped:** phase-only continuous connection as a positive hard-integrity or `Theta` switch source. **OPEN:** a UD-sourced generator for the seam/retained-environment state, its discrete event/singularity rule and eligibility, the bridge between internal edge link and `Theta` lift, and an independent OP03 target. No new autonomous dynamics is AUTO_LOCKed, no model-generated endpoints are passed off as independent, no physical correspondence is promoted. The attached `UD_GOVERNANCE_CRL2_SUBDIVISION_v1.0.md`, §§1–4, remains a governance proposal with non-constructor review pending. Physical promotion 0.\n"
