    "content": "# UD OP03 receipt-index eligibility and typed-seat amendment v0.1\n\n**11 October 2026 UTC · development addendum · physical promotion 0.**\n\n## Source hierarchy and question\n\n`UD_OPEN_SYSTEM_HAMMING_BUDGET_RECEIPT_INDEX_LAW_v0.2 (1).md` (30 August 2026, Library `libfile_8ea519b7af8881918c2d009ce74fe8d8`), §§1, 3–8, defines a conditional finite continuation index and a first-admissibility event rule. `UD_HAMMING_BUDGET_RECEIPT_INDEX_INDEPENDENT_AUDIT_v0.1.json` (30 August, `libfile_f8791a67b2a8819185cd7dd98d28504d`) independently reproduces rank and endpoint-optimizer algebra but explicitly says receipt construction and held-out performance remain conditional. `UD_OP03_INDEPENDENT_EVENT_ACQUISITION_PROTOCOL_v0.2_RECEIPT_INDEX.md` (4 September, `libfile_e56ff2964c8881918c6564d57e9a6a17`), §§Event boundary–Rollback, and its JSON schema (`libfile_65d6302675688191baefd0a7d73d6e20`) supersede the older v0.1 intake for receipt-index claims. `UD_OP03_AUTHENTICATED_HELD_OUT_REPLAY_SOURCE_GATE_v0.2.md` (14 September, `libfile_32f759d285608191a746627e198f7be7`), §§0–5, records source-blocked independent replay.\n\nThe previous [C1 frame-boundary capture](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-11T012338Z-codex-frame-boundary-fc4d4c2a) accurately scoped the frame extractor but did not account for the later v0.2 receipt-index event rule. This addendum **scope-amends** that remaining-gate statement. Its two tests ask whether the v0.2 rule distinguishes an executable null calculation from a switch, and whether a unique optimizer endpoint respects the independently typed output seat ledger.\n\n## Native (C_1) transport source boundary\n\nOn the filled oriented tetrahedron with Euclidean chain support metric, let (B_1:C_1\\to C_0), (B_2:C_2\\to C_1), and let (A) be the native skew Hodge–Dirac generator on (C_0\\oplus C_1\\oplus C_2\\oplus C_3). The attached `UD_COEFFICIENT_PROVENANCE_LEDGER_v0.39(2).md`, Q169, is the source for the global generator (local SHA-256 `1281aa8454013fbbdbcf8ada07af0aefe81014003f25a27f3929ad43afffae63`). Direct incidence gives (B_1^TB_1+B_2B_2^T=4I_6). If (c_1\\in C_1) and (Ac_1\\in C_1), then (B_1c_1=0=B_2^Tc_1), hence\n\n\\[\n4\\lVert c_1\\rVert^2=\\lVert B_1c_1\\rVert^2+\\lVert B_2^Tc_1\\rVert^2=0,\n\\qquad c_1=0.\n\\]\n\n**EXACT, scoped:** the native 15-dimensional generator has no nonzero invariant subspace lying entirely inside (C_1). Consequently simply restricting this generator to an autonomous six-dimensional Markovian (C_1) state is unlawful. An operator action on six source-labelled probes could be recorded as a diagnostic, but compressing each step does not give the composed event transport: at (s=\\pi/4), (P_1e^{sA}\\iota_1=0_6), so the product of two compressed steps is (0_6), while (P_1e^{2sA}\\iota_1=-I_6). The [earlier projection audit](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-11T010749Z-codex-native-projection-c9c95ae7) has the same typed warning. This rules out the **naive Markovian restriction**, not every possible sourced (C_1) transfer or memory-enriched lineage construction.\n\n`UD_RELATIVE_FRAME_FROM_C1_EXECUTION_v0.7.md` (30 August, `libfile_197ff0fbc504819185ef21e9e3ed083f`), §§0–5, takes a source-complete pre-event (C_1) transfer as an input and extracts a frame when boundary covariance passes. The attached v0.39(2) global generator does not supply the missing native map from its coupled 15-dimensional evolution to that input. **OPEN_GATED:** give an actual ordered six-basis input/output action with source/target frames and history, or a memory/paired-history construction with its composition and lineage certificates. Keep the primitive local edge (U_e), chain compression, and frame residual distinct.\n\n## Counterexample 1: first admissibility can select a null self-loop\n\nWork in the fixed identity frame (r=e), with (\\Theta=\\mathbb F_2^3), (\\bar\\theta^-=000), pair-integrity (T=(1,1,1)), and source-complete coordinate obligations