producer identity, pre-frozen (C_1) action, lineage/seat map, viability and burden receipts, prediction hash before access, and sealed endpoint frame/Θ. A current Library title/content search for OP03 histories and sealed endpoints surfaced protocols, synthetic controls, and the v0.2 source-blocked gate; targeted code searches on the UD GitHub default branch for `pre_event.jsonl`, `outcomes.jsonl`, `observed_theta_plus`, `lineage_equivalence_receipts`, and `sealed` returned no matches. Those search scopes do not prove global nonexistence. The previously documented v0.9 corpus is synthetic and does not exercise the v0.2 receipt-index law (`UD_OP03_JOINT_REPLAY_AND_RECEIPT_INDEX_RECONCILIATION_v0.1.md`, `libfile_ad8e43dd4cb48191936989f9069ed00e`, §§Receipt-index–Next replay).\n\n**NO_DATA / NOT_RUN:** no independent endpoints were exposed and no frozen OP03 scorer was run. The v0.2 protocol remains the intake, with this addendum's null and seat-compatibility findings frozen **before any future target exposure**. If targets already existed elsewhere, the amendment must be treated as exploratory against those targets; a fresh independently governed cohort would be required for a confirmatory test.\n\n## Disposition and reopening conditions\n\n**EXACT:** the (C_1) non-invariance and compression-composition obstruction; both finite v0.2 counterexamples under stated coordinate-seat assumptions; rank-nullity index identity is preserved. **CANDIDATE:** v0.2.1 no-op event typing and seat-compatibility gate. **OPEN_GATED:** native source-complete (C_1) producer or lawful paired history, independent typed lineage-to-seat construction, and independently sealed target history. No external physical correspondence or predictive validation is established. Physical promotion remains 0, independent review pending.\n"
