    "content": "# OP03 observed-frame and seat-source input contract v0.1 — candidate\n\n**11 October 2026 UTC · development — no registry entry · physical promotion 0.** Appends to acquisition protocol v0.2 and null/seat candidate v0.2.1; neither source is overwritten.\n\n## Independent pre-event producer\n\nBefore opening endpoints, commit producer identity, version, code hash, source and custody chronology, ordered candidate/null windows, frozen previous completed \\(\\Theta\\) event index, and one fixed frame route per producer. The memory route must provide the full 12-by-12 observed transfer \\(O\\) and same-history co-moving \\(M\\), oriented input/output incidence and basis, exact arithmetic, and all six-basis probes. Require the block and boundary certificate in `REPORT.md`; record hold on failure. A directly produced six-dimensional \\(C_1\\) transfer may instead use the original v0.7 gate, with no post-target route switching.\n\nFor each candidate freeze \\(\\theta^-\\), the ordered receipt maps \\(F,A_{\\rm src},A_{\\rm ren}\\), lineage IDs, predecessor/equivalence and viability certificates, pair-seat images, pair integrity, burden history, source/sink/renewal types and target-independent eligibility. Compute \\(L^+\\), exact rank, coordinate support and the seat certificate. Coordinate-complete pass fixes \\(\\theta^+\\) only if every required open seat is intact. A non-coordinate output holds without a separately frozen typed address map. Calculate \\(a=\\bar\\theta^-\\oplus\\theta^+\\); mark `ADMISSIBLE_NO_CHANGE` if zero and `THETA_SWITCH` otherwise, including zero-index swaps. A no-change window retains the prior completed \\(\\Theta\\) event index.\n\n## Sealed endpoint and scoring\n\nHash the entire ordered pre-event prediction stream, hold reasons, null windows and code versions before target access. Separately seal source-independent observed full frame and \\(\\Theta\\) endpoints with acquisition and release timestamps and hashes. Score coverage, holds, frame, event/no-change, timing, index, pair address and full affine receipt separately. A valid in-domain mismatch fails the respective universal candidate claim. Exposed or selector-generated endpoints are invalid as confirmatory tests. Finite synthetic fixtures and the current exact verifier are controls only. No data available at freeze; target score NOT_RUN.\n\n## Producer dependency and rollback\n\nThe native \\(C_1\\) memory law supplies \\(M\\) but not \\(O\\); v0.2 gives conditional receipt algebra but not a native producer of viable lineage maps. Revise any dependency only by an add-only versioned amendment before a fresh cohort. Retain exact algebra if a proposed input-to-event correspondence fails. Governance proposal `UD_GOVERNANCE_CRL2_SUBDIVISION_v1.0.md` permits at most CRL-2a for this constructor-authored bridge until non-constructor adversarial review and custodian ruling; no rung promotion here.\n"
