    "size_bytes": 7032,
    "content": "# UD observed-frame and lineage-seat producer audit v0.1\n\n**11 October 2026 UTC. Development — no registry entry. Physical promotion 0.**\n\n## Source and claim boundary\n\nThe attached `UD_COEFFICIENT_PROVENANCE_LEDGER_v0.39(2).md` (SHA-256 `1281aa8454013fbbdbcf8ada07af0aefe81014003f25a27f3929ad43afffae63`), Q165/Q169, defines the filled-tetrahedron Euclidean chain flow. `UD_RELATIVE_FRAME_FROM_C1_EXECUTION_v0.7.md` (30 August 2026, Library `libfile_197ff0fbc504819185ef21e9e3ed083f`), §§0–5, defines the oriented six-edge boundary frame gate. `UD_PREEVENT_RELATIVE_FRAME_SOURCE_LAW_v0.1.md` (30 August, `libfile_f5cc9aef39fc819180ce90b67b7ec4b5`), §§2,4–6, gives the conditional observed/co-moving route. `UD_OPEN_SYSTEM_HAMMING_BUDGET_RECEIPT_INDEX_LAW_v0.2` (30 August, `libfile_8ea519b7af8881918c2d009ce74fe8d8`), §§1,3–8, requires frozen pair-seat images, lineage, viability and integrity receipts. The prior [memory/seat capture](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/tree/main/captures/2026-10-11T014149Z-codex-memory-seat-b7043e45), report §§2–4 and candidate protocol v0.2.1, supplies the exact 12D native lift and no-op handling. The attached `UD_GOVERNANCE_CRL2_SUBDIVISION_v1.0.md`, §§1–4 (proposal), keeps a bridge proposal at CRL-2a until non-constructor review; no such review is claimed here.\n\n## Conditional 12D-to-6D frame certificate\n\nOn a fixed oriented filled tetrahedron let \\(q=c_1\\in C_1\\cong\\mathbb Q^6\\), \\(p=\\dot c_1\\in C_1\\), \\(W=C_1\\oplus C_1\\), and the native quarter-step map\n\n\\[\nM=\\begin{pmatrix}0&I_6/2\\\\-2I_6&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad M^{-1}=-M.\n\\]\n\nSuppose an independent producer freezes a **source-complete observed transfer** \\(O:W^{\\rm in}\\to W^{\\rm out}\\) and certifies the same anchored co-moving native map \\(M\\) before target exposure. Form the typed residual \\(R=OM^{-1}\\). The memory-frame gate requires the exact block identity\n\n\\[\nR=\\begin{pmatrix}Q&0\\\\0&Q\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad Q:C_1^{\\rm in}\\to C_1^{\\rm out}.\n\\]\n\nApply the v0.7 extractor to \\(Q\\), not to the 12D residual: \\(\\widehat P_0=(B_{1,\\rm out}QB_{1,\\rm in}^{T}+J_4)/4\\). Require \\(\\widehat P_0\\) exactly a permutation, \\(B_{1,\\rm out}Q=\\widehat P_0B_{1,\\rm in}\\), and \\(Q=\\rho_1(\\widehat P_0)\\). If all pass, a unique \\(r\\in S_4\\) is decoded. Otherwise return a typed hold, never a nearest frame. The second block and zero off-diagonal blocks are essential: \\(\\operatorname{diag}(I_6,\\rho_1(r))M\\) would fool a decoder inspecting only the \\(q\\) block.\n\n**EXACT conditional:** the gate recovers all 24 \\(S_4\\) frame fixtures and passes 576 two-sided input/output relabelings, including the quarter-step where the \\(q\\)-only transfer is zero. Under fixed labels the native \\(M\\) commutes with every lifted \\(S_4\\) action and supplies no nonidentity observed frame. The factor \\(O\\) is a required source, not a construction from \\(M\\). A change in the decoded frame is a receipt of frame change; a positive structural \\(\\Theta\\) switch still requires separate source and eligibility. This construction is a **conditional interface**, not an endogenous frame law.\n\n## Exact lineage-to-seat certificate\n\nLet the pre-event receipt producer supply \\(F:\\mathcal L^-\\to\\mathcal M_\\Theta\\), \\(A_{\\rm src},A_{\\rm ren}\\) with \\(\\mathcal M_\\Theta=\\mathbb Q^3\\) and ordered basis \\((e_A,e_B,e_C)\\). Let \\(L^+=\\operatorname{Im}[F\\ A_{\\rm src}\\ A_{\\rm ren}]\\). Define the coordinate support\n\n\\[\nS(L^+)=\\{p:\\text{the }p\\text{th coordinate functional is nonzero on }L^+\\}.\n\\]\n\nThe smallest coordinate subspace containing \\(L^+\\) is \\(E_S=\\operatorname{span}\\{e_p:p\\in S(L^+)\\}\\). Therefore\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{L^+=E_S\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\dim L^+=|S(L^+)|.}\n\\]\n\nThis is a source-typed certificate when the underlying lineage maps, equivalences, viability and pair-seat images were frozen independently of \\(\\theta^+\\). On pass, the **unique** coordinate endpoint obeys \\(\\theta_p^+=0\\iff p\\in S(L^+)\\), subject to open-seat pair integrity. On failure, dimension determines only the Hamming shell; `SEAT_MAP_MISSING` holds unless a separate frozen address map is supplied. For example \\(L^+=\\operatorname{span}(e_A+e_B)\\) has rank one and support two, so neither singleton is selected by rank. The certificate is invariant under a change of lineage basis and covariant under the \\(S_3\\) pair relabeling. It uses no numerical threshold or fitted burden. The source v0.2 burden optimizer remains a conditional shell comparison; in coordinate-complete cases it cannot overrule the receipt's typed address without an explicit versioned amendment.\n\nThe verifier constructs all 40 distinct subspaces generated by subsets of nonzero vectors in \\(\\{-1,0,1\\}^3\\), including all eight coordinate subspaces, and checks the criterion and six relabelings for each (240 checks). This finite census supports implementation, while the dimension proof covers all rational subspaces. The receipt producer itself is **not** derived from the native Hodge–Dirac flow; constitutive lineage/viability laws remain OPEN.\n\n## Acquisition and freeze status\n\n`UD_OP03_INDEPENDENT_EVENT_ACQUISITION_PROTOCOL_v0.2_RECEIPT_INDEX.md` (30 August, `libfile_e56ff2964c8881918c6564d57e9a6a17`), “Pre-event frame packet” through “Hidden target packet,” and `UD_OP03_AUTHENTICATED_HELD_OUT_REPLAY_SOURCE_GATE_v0.2.md` (14 September, `libfile_32f759d285608191a746627e198f7be7`), §§0–5, require independent pre-event and sealed endpoint packets. The Library title search for OP03/held-out/pre-event files through 11 October found protocols, prior captures, synthetic fixtures and a purpose-built bench specification whose status is `INDEPENDENT_ENGINE_AND_REAL_ACQUISITION_PENDING`. Four targeted GitHub default-branch code searches (`pre_event.jsonl`, `outcomes.jsonl`, `observed_theta_plus`, `lineage_equivalence_receipts`) returned zero hits. These scopes