    "content": "# OP03 independent producer and reviewer requests v0.1\n\n**11 October 2026 UTC · unaddressed, unsent · STATUS: SOURCE_BLOCKED / REVIEW_PENDING.**\n\n## Source lock\n\nRepository `ud-tetra/UD`, commit `285179d44bed55cb9ae09d10d7e8f0ca1ccc3fd7`:\n\n- [Independent producer handoff v0.1](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/285179d44bed55cb9ae09d10d7e8f0ca1ccc3fd7/captures/2026-10-11T020241Z-codex-op03-producer-handoff-23f7e091/PROVIDER_HANDOFF_v0.1.md), §§Assignment–Return checklist; Git blob `c58224403672e228206b2513d16fcc3578558169`.\n- [Candidate guard v0.2.1](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/285179d44bed55cb9ae09d10d7e8f0ca1ccc3fd7/captures/2026-10-11T014149Z-codex-memory-seat-b7043e45/PROTOCOL_v0.2.1_CANDIDATE.md), §§Inputs–Rollback; blob `ceb657fdaa5966447117f712084539548ff632ec`.\n- [Source input contract v0.1](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/285179d44bed55cb9ae09d10d7e8f0ca1ccc3fd7/captures/2026-10-11T015458Z-codex-source-bridge-8e19b473/INPUT_CONTRACT_v0.1_CANDIDATE.md), §§Independent pre-event producer–Producer dependency; blob `f1abcb3a02fd3e0ed401cabfd3a463adbe8bd2e8`.\n- [Source audit v0.1](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/285179d44bed55cb9ae09d10d7e8f0ca1ccc3fd7/captures/2026-10-11T015458Z-codex-source-bridge-8e19b473/REPORT.md), §§Conditional 12D-to-6D frame certificate–Acquisition and freeze status; blob `6d2ff0b2ff3f77e75c2de16c109449a09a7a743c`.\n\nThe frozen acquisition protocol v0.2 and authenticated source gate v0.2 remain upstream. This packet does not amend either or authorize target release. The source audit reports no qualified independent endpoint and physical promotion 0.\n\n## Request A — independent event and endpoint producer\n\n**Subject:** OP03 independent K4 event acquisition — source and endpoint custody\n\nI am seeking an independently governed producer for a target-blind OP03 test. The exact handoff and source contract are linked above. Would your group assess feasibility and, if feasible, commit its own event/measurement engine, code hash, frame route, chronology, eligibility and exclusion rules *before* endpoint acquisition?\n\nThe return needs all consecutive candidate **and null** windows on one labeled, oriented K4 carrier. Pre-event packets must include the ordered source-complete edge transport or the declared observed/co-moving 12D route; pre-state, lineage and pair-seat maps; viability, integrity and burden receipts; and enough raw arithmetic for independent recomputation. Keep a separate, sealed target lane with independently observed full relative frame and full three-bit Θ endpoint for the **same** windows. A custodian must prevent target release until the UD prediction stream is sealed and hashed. Please report unavailable fields as typed holds and record who authored each source and target component.\n\nThe existing synthetic fixtures and one-pair Xi benchmark are controls or separate claims, not qualifying full OP03 endpoints. A feasibility decline or an impossibility of independent endpoint observation is a valuable explicit return. No physical-law claim is being made from a successful finite cohort.\n\n## Request B — non-constructor adversarial reviewer\n\n**Subject:** Independent pretarget review — OP03 v0.2.1 source/seat decision guard\n\nPlease review the pinned v0.2.1 guard and input contract without participating in their construction. Return a signed or attributable versioned review with the code/commit reviewed, conflicts or prior involvement, exact counterexamples or pass conditions, and whether each pre-event field can be produced without reading the endpoint. Please review before any new target cohort is opened; a later correction is exploratory for exposed data.\n\nSpecific challenges:\n\n1. Check the typed 12D residual `R = O M^{-1}`: both diagonal 6D blocks must be the **same** signed-edge action, off-diagonal blocks zero, and the oriented boundary extractor must certify an exact S4 image. Probe a different second block, a singular q-only quarter-step, and relabeled input/output bases.\n2. Check the coordinate-seat theorem with independently frozen maps `F`, `A_src`, `A_ren`: `L+ = Im[F A_src A_ren]`, support `S(L+)`, and the equivalence `L+ = E_S` iff `rank(L+) = |S|`. Test non-coordinate lines, missing pair integrity, coincident lineage IDs and a seat map constructed from the hidden Θ endpoint. Reject hidden endpoint leakage rather than completing a nearest seat.\n3. Check `a = complement(theta-minus) XOR theta-plus`, including an admissible no-change case, a zero-index seat swap, frame-only change, holds, and consecutive null windows. Verify that only a completed Θ switch advances the prior-event index and that coverage and first-switch denominators retain nulls.\n4. Check whether the source law actually produces exposure, lineage, viability and pair address before target access. Algebraic covariance and the 13,824-case constructor-authored guard census do not certify a native occurrence law or independent prediction.\n5. State which claim would fail on an in-domain frame, seat, timing, switch/no-switch or affine-receipt mismatch. Distinguish a proof, a finite implementation check, an independently acquired endpoint and a physical bridge.\n\nAn adverse review should preserve the narrower exact algebra and identify the smallest counterexample and the assumptions that fail. No CRL promotion is requested from a review alone; any governance decision also needs a separate custodian ruling.\n\n## Custody and dispatch log\n\n| Gate | Current state | Required next record |\n|---|---|---|\n| Producer identity and independent authoring | OPEN | Named person/group accepts scope and supplies producer/custodian roles |\n| Reviewer identity and non-construction declaration | OPEN | Named reviewer accepts scope and declares involvement |\n| Pre-event source and prediction seals | NOT_RUN | Ordered files, chronology and hashes |\n| Hidden full endpoints and score | NOT_RUN | Independent endpoint seal, then predic