    "size_bytes": 4328,
    "content": "# Separate AI audit of bounded K4 comparison model v0.1\n\n**12 October 2026 UTC.** Separate AI implementation and proof review, **not independent human/nonconstructor peer review**, not a CRL promotion or physical evidence. The audited source is [bounded K4 pre-event comparison model v0.1, §§Declared objects–Adversarial results](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-12T001121Z-codex-k4-pre-event-40c08e54/MODEL.md), with [original verifier](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-12T001121Z-codex-k4-pre-event-40c08e54/verify.py) and [results](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-12T001121Z-codex-k4-pre-event-40c08e54/results.json).\n\nThe separate `audit_k4_separate_ai.py` uses a packed per-pair evolution and edge permutation implementation; it imports no original verifier code. It passed **5,120** exhaustive local admissible states with multistep budget/stabilization checks, **24,000** S4 comparisons using eight mixed-pair fixture patterns across 125 theta/integrity states, and all **64** edge-mask outputs. `audit_results.json` is its result. No counterexample to the scoped model invariant or capacity theorem was found.\n\n**Proof check.** An open pair has both edge integrity bits one, so neither edge can fail under the rule. A closed pair can open only when both pre-integrity bits are one and no same-pair failure occurs, preserving the open-pair invariant. Every executed pulse removes precisely its own one-use fuel bit, bounding total structural pulses by the initial sum `B_0 <= 21`. The relabeling action preserves the unordered opposite-edge partition and applies the same local rule to each transformed edge and pair. With fixed visible `theta=C=T=1`, phase zero, and all other fuels fixed at zero, varying the six closure-fuel bits produces `h'=1 XOR b^C`; the 64 outputs require at least 64 distinguishable source states for a deterministic selector at that visible base. The **full** pre-state differs between these examples because its fuel differs.\n\n**Clarification to v0.1 wording (no rule change):** An off-phase (`z=1`) step has no pulses but can be followed by a firing on-phase. Permanent structural stabilization follows once a **complete on-phase** (`z=0`) has no eligible pulse, because the next off-phase leaves the structural/fuel registers fixed and returns to the same on-phase configuration; it also follows once all fuel is exhausted. The finite-budget argument alone rules out infinitely many pulses, but does not make every arbitrary no-pulse step terminal. This corrects any overly broad reading of “once no pulse is possible” in v0.1 §Exact conditional proofs, item 2; the formula and source code are unchanged.\n\n**Limit:** The audit validates a stipulated finite automaton. It does not derive its phase, fuels, pair/edge bridge, edge-map update from native UD packets, or demonstrate physical timing or a source-independent endpoint. It must not be called independent human review. Physical promotion remains **0**.\n\n## Critical reading of the new source-projection theorem\n\nThe same separate AI reviewer checked `THEOREM.md` and `verify.py`. The singleton-fiber factorization proof and fixed-`A,c` pre-event jet corollary are valid under their stated assumptions. The reviewer identified two overreach risks, corrected in the version captured here:\n\n1. The distinct `xi=000` and `xi=111` completions are **hypothetical type-correct** external inputs. The source addendum does not demonstrate two actual provider receipts for one physical preparation. The theorem now asserts logical underdetermination by the present conditional interface, not physical dual-history reachability.\n2. The edge witness keeps only reduced `(C,T)` inputs fixed. It now concludes a no-go for prediction from those reduced inputs, while determination from a richer native cochain state remains OPEN.\n\nThe stochastic examples distinguish `None` (no valid receipt, operational deferral) from an applied `xi=000` receipt and are described as fiberwise formal distributions, not a global UD kernel or physical rate. The new verifier passes **1,536** pair-action cases, **72** conditional flip-distribution checks and **216** receipt-availability checks. This remains a separate AI critique, not independent human review or CRL promotion.\n"
