rect-Theta receipt\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\xi_{n,p}=\\mathbf 1\\{d_p(c_n)d_p(\\hat c_{n+1})<0\\},\\qquad\n\\Theta_{n+1}=\\Theta_n\\oplus\\xi_n.}\n\\]\n\nHere `xi=000` is a computed zero-flip receipt, not missing data. Missing/invalid `c_n` instead has status `DEFERRED`, with no scored predicted event. Endpoint zero on either score gives `xi_p=0` by **stipulated tie convention**, and must be tagged `DEGENERATE` separately. The law detects a **strict endpoint sign reversal**, not every continuous crossing inside the interval; two unresolved crossings can alias to zero. Simultaneous qualifying pairs all flip in one batch, with no exclusive contact priority. Pre-event `Theta_n` does not enter the score, but sets the final pair endpoint. This is a causal, deterministic formal model given its initial state and imposed clock.\n\nFor the **specific pair lift** of the admitted direct-Theta report, if a separate predeclared fixed-transport certificate covers a window, set `C_{e,n}=1-Theta_{n,p(e)}`, `T_{e,n+1}=T_{e,n}` and compute `h_{e,n+1}=C_{e,n+1}T_{e,n}`. This predicts only pair-constant closure factors filtered by fixed typed edge `T`; it does not derive a six-edge transport update or all 64 masks. If the certificate fails or is absent, report `EDGE_MASK_DEFERRED` even though the pair receipt is calculable. The gate `h_e` is a readout, not the input source score. No conflation of global `C_1` action with local edge map `U_e` is permitted.\n\n## Conditional mathematical consequences\n\n**EXACT under the declared rule.** For every rational `c`, `I-A/2` is invertible because `A` is real skew, and `Q_1^TQ_1=I`. Thus the discrete chain norm is conserved, but this is not a support renewal law. An oriented vertex relabeling acts by signed permutation on each chain group and intertwines `B_k`, `A` and `Q_h`. The square of each edge coordinate discards its orientation sign; the three unordered opposite-edge sums permute by the matching `S4→S3` action. Therefore `xi(gc)=P_g xi(c)`, and