    "content": "# UD packet-action event-source and renewal audit v0.1\n\n**12 October 2026 UTC. EXACT conditional two-branch kernel counterexample; NO-GO deriving a unique switch schedule from the available action/admissibility statements. OPEN native pair receipt, feedback/renewal and physical clock. Physical promotion 0.** This preserves the prior continuous contrast candidate as a candidate; no result is promoted to an autonomous UD law.\n\n## Source and status lock\n\nThe attached March 2026 `distinction_dynamics_manuscript.pdf` (SHA-256 `909ac4bfbb07ab815d15463648278877a7452989797589bf630564a0afa9f1ef`) is a **historical packet proposal**, not the current accepted event source. Its §§2,4 define packet variables `X_i=(rho_i,theta_i,chi_i)`, link transport `U_ij`, and a proposed action consisting of loop-holonomy, burden and orientation-mismatch terms. Its §13 gives an illustrative Monte Carlo loop: choose a random node or edge, propose a local `X_i` or `U_ij` change, compute `Delta S`, and accept with `min(1,exp(-Delta S/T))`. It does not specify a proposal distribution, all admissible moves, graph-update/renewal dynamics, a physical attempt clock, or a map from its local `chi_i` to the current K4 pair bits `Theta_p`. Those are separately typed.\n\nThe current [Paper I review draft v1.1.1 §7.4](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_I_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md) expressly leaves the pre-event binary offset/source outside its exact conditional map. The supplied `UD_COEFFICIENT_PROVENANCE_LEDGER_v0.39(2).md` (22 August 2026, SHA-256 `1281aa8454013fbbdbcf8ada07af0aefe81014003f25a27f3929ad43afffae63`) marks Q153's burden flux/source law as open, Q158's source/sink as a *residual receipt*, Q156/Q167/Q173's masks/currents as conditional on gates, and Q178/Q179's open-system renewal terms as unsourced. The [current UD portal](https://tetrahedral-packet-complexes.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/) lists Papers I–III v1.1.1 and physical promotion 0. The earlier [continuous contrast v0.2](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-12T135643Z-codex-continuous-admission-0575daf6/PROTOCOL.md) is an explicit comparator, not a packet-source derivation.\n\nThe attachment `packet_modulation_layer.md` and `Gap2_FINAL_Finite_Genesis.png` were unavailable this turn; neither was read. The available seam/transport and equation `.md` snapshots are one-line placeholders. The full-repository zip contains similarly short placeholder snapshots; it provides no executable packet source law. The two PDFs and ledger were inspected as source data, with present-version precedence assigned to the current reviewed Paper I and ledger.\n\n## Conditional rate/clock counterexample inside the historical packet proposal\n\nThe displayed March action is\n\n\\[\nS_{\\rm packet}=\\sum_C\\kappa\\operatorname{Tr}(I-U_C)\n+\\sum_i\\lambda(\\rho_i-\\rho_0)^2\n+\\sum_{\\langle ij\\rangle}\\eta(\\theta_i-\\theta_j)^2.\n\\]\n\n**Object and assumptions.** Hold graph, all `U`, `rho`, and `theta` fixed; consider one local binary branch `chi∈{0,1}`. **Condition on both `chi` values and a `chi`-only proposal being admissible** under some future explicit grammar. The displayed action contains no `chi`, so `Delta S=0` for this move and Metropolis acceptance equals 1 for any `T>0`. The source does not specify how often that move is proposed. For any `r∈[0,1]`, define a symmetric pre-event proposal kernel per **attempt**, independently across attempts,\n\n\\[\nK_r=\\begin{pmatrix}1-r&r\\\\r&1-r\\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\n`r` is an illustrative **unsourced proposal probability**, not a UD coefficient or measured rate. Both `r=1/4` and `r=1/2` have the same displayed action, unit acceptance for a proposed branch flip, symmetry/detailed balance and uniform stationary distribution `(1/2,1/2)`. Yet the expected first-flip attempt counts are `4` and `2`; their three-attempt **strict null-window** probabilities are `(3/4)^3=27/64` and `(1/2)^3=1/8`. Their probabilities of an **unchanged endpoint after three attempts**, allowing two flips, are `9/16` and `1/2`. Thus equal stationary states and the same action/acceptance do not identify an event schedule, null frequency, or first-switch timing. `verify.py` checks all statements in exact `Fraction` arithmetic and compares powers through ten steps. An attempt index is not seconds.\n\n**NO-GO scope.** This is a conditional logical counterexample to inferring a unique *primitive branch* update from the historical action plus acceptance formula. It does **not** prove that actual UD admits `chi`-only moves, that `chi` equals the current K4 `Theta`, or that either Markov kernel occurs physically. If an independently sourced proposal/eligibility rule prohibits these moves, that defines a narrower new branch; the action alone still did not supply that rule. Identifying `chi` with `Theta`, or inferring the pair flip receipt `xi`, would require a separate typed carrier/readout bridge.\n\n## The source-complete feedback/renewal dependency cut\n\nA future autonomous packet/defect law must supply, before endpoint exposure:\n\n| Required typed item | Current status | What is needed to predict switches |\n|---|---|---|\n| State/carrier | Paper I closed K4 chains; historical `X_i,U_ij` proposal; ledger support/burden | Common labeled carrier and map from packet/defect variables to pair `Theta` and six local `C_e,T_e` |\n| Proposal/admission | Historical Metropolis acceptance only, Paper I §7.4 receipt source OPEN | Explicit admissible move support and a normalized attempt/kernel law or deterministic event generator, including symmetry ties and simultaneous contacts |\n| Feedback and renewal | Ledger Q153/Q158 and Q178/Q179 source/sink laws OPEN | Pre-event constitutive packet flux, support/burden source and sink, gate transition and post-event state map; initial/boundary data and conservation balance |\n| Clock | Paper I `s` dimensionless; historical Monte Carlo attempt step | Source mapping from attempt/event parameter to any physical time, with units, calibration and uncertainty |\n| Endpoint/readout | Conditional `Theta` receipt and `h_e=C_eT_e` | Causal `xi`, closure and local transport update generated before targets; no endpoint-derived source variable |\n| Evaluation | OP03 producer handoff v0.1 reports zero complete targets | Independent same-carrier ordered positive **and null** windows, sealed pre-state/target chronology, baseline and falsifier |\n\nUnder the closed no-feedback continuous contrast v0.2, an active pair has two recurring switches per `π/2` internal period; affected `Theta` and pair-lift closure never terminally settle. To obtain settling **within that specific candidate**, at least one of its continuing fixed flow, no-feedback assumption, unbounded horizon, or every-crossing admission axiom must change. A source/sink or feedback law is a plausible repair, not derived by this necessity statement. Merely appending a fuel bit or gate whose initial value encodes a desired endpoint is not a source derivation.\n\n## Execution and disposition\n\n**Executed:** exact two-kernel comparison and manuscript/ledger source audit. **Not executed:** independent same-carrier event score, hardware/physical clock calibration, packet proposal/renewal derivation. A synthetic two-state branch kernel is a mathematical witness, **not** an OP03 target corpus or a reproduction of observed switches. No AUTO_LOCK of a source rule, no CRL advancement, physical promotion **0**. The independent provider assessment is captured separately in this versioned package if available; a missing provider is recorded as `NOT_RUN` rather than replaced with generated positives.\n"
