    "content": "# Gibbs-flag receipt apparatus and its joint error state\n\n2026-10-13. Benjamin Walker Mayes, AI-assisted development. Development — no registry entry. Physical promotion 0; independent review OPEN.\n\n## Outcome and source qualification\n\nAn explicit candidate apparatus now supplies a joint receipt-error state, including a shared-error mechanism, instead of merely assuming an error distribution. Its unitary, flag Gibbs state, marginalization, joint moments and accuracy bounds are checked exactly.\n\nThis is a conditional apparatus derivation, not a native UD source closure. The supplied carrier_definition.md, coherence_equation.md and master_action.md are placeholders; ledger G05/G06 still do not supply an apparatus Hamiltonian, its thermal preparation, calibrated gaps or coupling law. Native face projector A=P_f anchors the signal. The flag state and controlled interactions below are newly declared physical candidates. G is unused.\n\n## 1. Declare state, Hamiltonian and interaction\n\nHold the binary carrier observable A with the prior four-incidence coupling suspension. Let R=0 or 1 denote its held eigenlabel. Use three degenerate blank receipt bits S_1,S_2,S_3.\n\nSupply one shared flag C and three private flags Z_i with Hamiltonian\n\n\\[\nH_F=\\Delta_c n_C+\\Delta_p\\sum_{i=1}^3 n_{Z_i}.\n\\]\n\nAt temperature T, declare the initially independent Gibbs flag state\n\n\\[\n\\tau_F=\\tau_c\\otimes\\tau_p^{\\otimes3},\\quad\n\\tau_r=(1-r)|0\\rangle\\langle0|+r|1\\rangle\\langle1|,\n\\]\n\nwhere\n\n\\[\nc=\\frac1{1+e^{\\beta\\Delta_c}},\\qquad\np=\\frac1{1+e^{\\beta\\Delta_p}},\\quad\\beta=1/(k_BT).\n\\]\n\nFor each receipt apply carrier-to-receipt CNOT, private-flag-to-receipt CNOT, and shared-flag-to-receipt CNOT. They commute during acquisition because they have unchanged controls and target bit flips. Their combined action is\n\n\\[\nU|R,c,z,s\\rangle\n=|R,c,z,s\\oplus R\\mathbf1\\oplus c\\mathbf1\\oplus z\\rangle.\n\\]\n\nThe shared flag interacts with all three receipts; each private flag interacts only with its corresponding receipt. A product initial flag state therefore does not imply independent receipt errors. Correlation is generated by a shared control path.\n\nThe checker verifies the acquisition permutation and inverse on all source/flag/receipt basis states. With source held and receipt targets degenerate, these controlled operations commute with the free held-source-plus-flag Hamiltonian. Their ideal net free-energy expectation change is zero. Timing, target isolation, coupling switches, preparation and routing are additional controller resources.\n\nThe private/common flags model controlled perturbations of acquisition. They are an explicit realization of the declared noise channel; nothing here proves these perturbations are intrinsic to native UD or unavoidable in a physical recorder.\n\n## 2. Derive the joint state\n\nFrom blank receipts the recorded bits are\n\n\\[\nS_i=R\\oplus C\\oplus Z_i,\n\\qquad E_i=S_i\\oplus R=C\\oplus Z_i.\n\\]\n\nTracing the flag registers gives, conditional on R,\n\n\\[\n\\rho_{S|R}=\\sum_{e\\in\\{0,1\\}^3}w_e\n|R\\mathbf1\\oplus e\\rangle\\langle R\\mathbf1\\oplus e|,\n\\]\n\nwith k=sum_i e_i and\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{w_e=(1-c)p^k(1-p)^{3-k}\n+c\\,p^{3-k}(1-p)^k.}\n\\]\n\nAfter carrier uncopies, the receipt error-state diagonal is the same w_e on |e>. Equivalently,\n\n\\[\n\\rho_E=(1-c)\\tau_p^{\\otimes3}\n+c\\,X^{\\otimes3}\\tau_p^{\\otimes3}X^{\\otimes3}.\n\\]\n\nThe eight probabilities are nonnegative and sum to one. This is the apparatus's derived joint error state under the declared Gibbs preparation and interactions. The symbolic form precedes choosing test probabilities.\n\n## 3. Exact moments and majority\n\nWrite p_bar for each receipt marginal error, a for each pair joint error, b for the triple joint error. Direct marginalization gives\n\n\\[\n\\bar p=p+c(1-2p),\\quad a=p^2+c(1-2p),\n\\]\n\\[\nb=(1-c)p^3+c(1-p)^3.\n\\]\n\nThus the local flag probability p is not the receipt marginal p_bar when c is nonzero. The mean pair covariance is\n\n\\[\na-\\bar p^2=c(1-c)(1-2p)^2\\ge0.\n\\]\n\nUsing the exact majority identity,\n\n\\[\nm=3a-2b=(3p^2-2p^3)+c[1-2(3p^2-2p^3)].\n\\]\n\nThe checker independently obtains these moments from the full flag-state sum and verifies the earlier sharp bounds\n\n\\[\n\\max(0,2a-\\bar p)\\le b\\le\\min(a,1-3\\bar p+3a).\n\\]\n\nIn particular the shared perturbation creates a majority-error component that is not quadratically suppressed by independent private flags.\n\n## 4. Decision flag state and final-error test\n\nSupply four further independent Gibbs flag bits D_j with gap Delta_q and excitation q=1/(1+exp(beta Delta_q)). Couple them as target XOR controls after the three forward majority gates and the seed-copy gate. They give a parity fault\n\n\\[\nu_4=\\frac{1-(1-2q)^4}{2},\n\\quad p_{\\rm seed}=m+u_4-2mu_4.\n\\]\n\nThe replay explicitly enumerates both the sixteen acquisition flag states and sixteen decision flag states to verify this effective error. Reverse cleanup and downstream fanout are ideal, and storage uses the previously specified fresh independent Gibbs stream.\n\nFor the prior 32-update ideal-seed storage error e0, final error is exactly\n\n\\[\ne_{\\rm final}=e_0+(1-2e_0)p_{\\rm seed}.\n\\]\n\nTest points p=1/100 and q=1/10000 are declared Gibbs excitation probabilities, not measured UD values. They correspond to beta Delta_p=ln99 and beta Delta_q=ln9999 within this candidate model. These gap assignments are test inputs, not canonical UD constants.\n\n| Shared excitation c | Receipt pair joint error a | Exact final error | Exact model passes 1% | Broad robust gate passes |\n|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| 0 | 1/10000 | 0.00992358 | yes | yes |\n| 1/100000 | 549/5000000 | 0.00993338 | yes | yes |\n| 1/20000 | 149/1000000 | 0.00997259 | yes | no |\n| 1/10000 | 99/500000 | 0.01002160 | no | no |\n\nPassing and failing comparisons are exact rational checks. A failed sufficient bound does not prove that the particular apparatus fails: the c=1/20000 row demonstrates this distinction. Its exact joint state contains triple coincidences which the broader bound conservatively discards.\n\n## 5. Two different shared-error ceilings\n\nLet s*=(1/100−e0)/(1−2e0). Without relying on decision independence, the sufficient gate 3a+4q<=s* gives\n\n\\[\nc\\le\\frac{s_*-4q-3p^2}{3(1-2p)}\n\\approx2.567950424\\times10^{-5}.\n\\]\n\nFor the fully specified independent decision flags, use the exact u4 and m. The exact passing region is\n\n\\[\nc\\le\\frac{s_*-u_4-(1-2u_4)(3p^2-2p^3)}\n{(1-2u_4)[1-2(3p^2-2p^3)]}\n\\approx7.796483800\\times10^{-5}.\n\\]\n\nBoth are conditional source requirements, with exact fractions in results.json. The first offers a guarantee under a broader decision-error class; the second depends on the explicitly prepared product decision state. UD must select or bound actual flag gaps and interactions before either becomes a native prediction.\n\n## 6. Energy, entropy, renewal and latency\n\nThe eight flag occupations are unchanged by their controlled-X interactions, so their marginal energies do not change. Receipt and decision targets are degenerate during those operations. Ideal net acquisition/decision heat and endpoint work are zero under the held-source control assumptions. Pure blank targets and the clock still supply resources.\n\nFor a fixed classical source label, receipt entropy grows from zero to H(w). The flags retain their original marginal entropy, while the combined unitary preserves total entropy. Receipt/flag correlations account for the local increase: I(receipts:flags|R)=H(w). Thus this explicit apparatus again shows that local record entropy need not equal heat divided by T. It does not close the horizon Clausius identification.\n\nBlind workspace reset must use H(w), not 3h(p_bar). The output garbage also depends on decision flags. Their joint state and correlations determine any accessible-side-information reduction. The pure-blank reset protocol remains open; its free-energy bound is not a finite exact preparation recipe.\n\nAfter use, matched-energy swaps with eight fresh Gibbs flag cells restore the required independent flag state, exporting correlations into the outgoing cells. These swaps need no net free-energy change of matched pairs. They require a fresh source and routing. A finite closed flag bank is not made cyclic by this export. Incoming energy inventory is Delta_c c+3 Delta_p p+4 Delta_q q, not extra dissipated work.\n\nThe apparatus also changes primitive locality and timing. Decomposing every declared flag interaction into separate CNOTs adds six acquisition flag gates and four decision flag gates to the earlier twenty-four-gate sequence. The explicit decomposed write therefore has 34 primitive gates and a 23-gate carrier hold, before eleven memory fanout gates complete it. Refresh/reset durations are additional. The accuracy table fixes 32 storage updates after the completed write; it does not reuse the previous 44-slot common-deadline schedule. A combined multi-control pulse could reduce gate count only by declaring a different interaction and duration.\n\n## Disposition\n\nDERIVED under declared apparatus: full joint error state; private/shared correlation mechanism; exact moments; decision flag parity; passing and failing bounds; thermal energy and correlation bookkeeping. OPEN: native selection of flag Hamiltonians, preparations and couplings; calibrated clocks, implementation losses and physical reset; apparatus area, extensive record density and horizon normalization.\n\nThe source task is now specific: recover a UD-authored law for the apparatus gaps and shared coupling, or derive those quantities in a new source programme. Native incidence algebra and the supplied placeholders do not determine them. No ledger, registry, site or repository was changed. Physical promotion 0; independent review OPEN. Gap2_FINAL_Finite_Genesis.png was unavailable and unused.\n"
