    "size_bytes": 9860,
    "content": "<header class=\"funding-header\">\n  <p class=\"eyebrow\">Contribution · Independent theoretical research</p>\n  <h1>Contribution</h1>\n  <p class=\"funding-lead\">Help strengthen Unified Dynamics through mathematical scrutiny, scientific analysis, reproducible code and practical support.</p>\n  <p>Mathematicians, scientists, research software contributors and independent peer reviewers are invited to volunteer their time on a clearly defined task. A checked proof, a counterexample, a corrected calculation or a sharper statement of an open question can all move the work forward.</p>\n  <div class=\"funding-actions\"><a class=\"home-button primary\" href=\"https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/issues/new?title=Contribution%20offer&amp;body=Area%20of%20expertise%3A%0A%0AArtifact%20or%20task%20of%20interest%3A%0A%0AProposed%20scope%20and%20availability%3A%0A%0APreferred%20acknowledgment%3A%0A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Offer a contribution</a><a class=\"home-button secondary\" href=\"#/contribution?section=first-task\">Choose a first task</a></div>\n  <p class=\"funding-status\">Benjamin Walker Mayes · Independent research · Physical promotion remains 0</p>\n</header>\n\n<section id=\"ways-to-contribute\">\n  <h2>Ways to contribute</h2>\n  <div class=\"funding-options\">\n    <article class=\"funding-option\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Mathematics</p><h3>Check, challenge or extend a result</h3><p>Review definitions, proofs and assumptions in discrete geometry, algebraic topology, spectral operators or dynamical systems. Find counterexamples, repair gaps, simplify arguments or compare a construction with established mathematics.</p></article>\n    <article class=\"funding-option\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Science</p><h3>Assess a proposed physical bridge</h3><p>Examine observables, units, source equations and measurement assumptions. Help define a falsifiable correspondence or review a proposed protocol against the evidence it would actually provide.</p></article>\n    <article class=\"funding-option\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Reproducibility</p><h3>Replay and improve the code</h3><p>Independently run a frozen calculation, check exact arithmetic and failure controls, document dependencies, or submit a small code improvement with a reproducible result receipt.</p></article>\n    <article class=\"funding-option\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Clarity and context</p><h3>Improve the research record</h3><p>Clarify notation, identify related work, supply an exact paper or source equation, review a manuscript section, or help make a bounded result easier for another researcher to inspect.</p></article>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<section id=\"volunteer-review\">\n  <h2>Volunteer independent peer review</h2>\n  <p>If you are a mathematician or scientist willing to scrutinize one defined claim, your help is welcome. Start with a specific artifact and version, agree a manageable scope, then assess the reasoning on its own merits.</p>\n  <ul><li><strong>Proof review:</strong> identify the hypotheses, check each inference and report missing steps or counterexamples.</li><li><strong>Independent reproduction:</strong> record the source version, environment, commands, results and any discrepancy.</li><li><strong>Scientific assessment:</strong> separate established mathematics from a proposed physical interpretation; examine testability, dimensional consistency and the required evidence.</li></ul>\n  <p>A useful review states what was checked, what remains unresolved and whether a correction is needed. Favorable and unfavorable findings are both valuable. Each review is recorded against its specific scope; the review summary and reviewer attribution are published with the reviewer's agreement. Constructor checks and independent reviews retain separate status.</p>\n  <p><a href=\"https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/issues/new?title=Volunteer%20review%20offer&amp;body=Relevant%20background%3A%0A%0AClaim%20and%20artifact%20version%3A%0A%0AProposed%20review%20scope%3A%0A%0AAvailability%3A%0A%0APreferred%20attribution%3A%0A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Offer a volunteer review</a> or <a href=\"https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/issues\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">join the repository discussion</a>.</p>\n</section>\n\n<section id=\"first-task\">\n  <h2>Choose a bounded first task</h2>\n  <ol class=\"funding-milestones\">\n    <li><strong>Review a finite operator calculation.</strong><span>Inspect the exact spectra and continuity package below. Check one declared A/B/C spectrum, a proof step or a frozen face-mask case, and return a short review with the artifact version.</span></li>\n    <li><strong>Audit the receipt and entropy assumptions.</strong><span><a href=\"#/doc/receiptGapFrontier20261013\">Review the receipt thermal-gap frontier</a>: check the corrected write/storage clock, the exact error bound or the physical-scale non-identifiability argument. Native gap selection and complete cyclic resource cost remain open.</span></li>\n    <li><strong>Recover a source equation.</strong><span>Connect one proposed correspondence to an exact paper, equation and stated assumptions. Distinguish the source result from the additional assumptions needed by UD.</span></li>\n    <li><strong>Return a small correction.</strong><span>Open an issue with a reproducible discrepancy or submit a focused pull request. Preserve the original record and explain the correction, its scope and how it was checked.</span></li>\n  </ol>\n</section>\n\n<section id=\"review-evidence\">\n  <h2>Evidence you can inspect now</h2>\n  <p>The finite review package includes a recovered September mathematical note and exact-arithmetic verifier. Its supplemental replay checks the declared A/B/C spectra, all 128 frozen face-gate masks and three deliberately introduced errors.</p>\n  <div class=\"funding-evidence\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Finite replay · v0.1</p><h3>Exact spectra and continuity on tetrahedral complexes</h3><p>Source snapshots, Python code, exact matrices, result receipts, reviewer questions and a SHA-256 manifest. Python standard library only.</p><div class=\"funding-actions\"><a class=\"home-button primary\" href=\"./releases/UD_REVIEW_REPLAY_v0.1.zip\" download>Download the replay package</a><a class=\"home-button secondary\" href=\"#/doc/fundingReplay\">Read the scope and results</a></div></div>\n  <p><strong>Review status:</strong> the existing replay is constructor-checked. Independent proof review, novelty assessment and proof-assistant verification remain outstanding. Frozen-mask continuity does not establish a gate-transition law or a physical result.</p>\n  <p><a href=\"#/doc/fundingReplayResults\">Exact result receipt</a> · <a href=\"#/doc/fundingReplayCode\">Supplemental verifier</a> · <a href=\"#/manuscript\">Research papers</a> · <a href=\"#/record\">Living research record</a> · <a href=\"https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">GitHub repository</a></p>\n</section>\n\n<section id=\"getting-started\">\n  <h2>How to get involved</h2>\n  <ol><li>Choose an artifact or propose a bounded task.</li><li>Open a contribution offer with your relevant background, proposed scope and availability.</li><li>Agree the scope, deliverable and attribution before beginning a coordinated review.</li><li>Return your proof notes, code, result receipt or review report with clear assumptions and limitations.</li></ol>\n  <p>Contributions can be small and self-contained. Attribution, acknowledgments and any coauthorship are agreed according to the contribution. Referrals to suitable researchers or reviewers are welcome.</p>\n  <div class=\"funding-actions\"><a class=\"home-button primary\" href=\"./source/contribution/UD_CONTRIBUTION_GUIDE_v0.1.md\" download>Download the contribution guide</a><a class=\"home-button secondary\" href=\"https://orcid.org/0009-0002-5813-0724\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Researcher profile</a></div>\n</section>\n\n<section id=\"practical-support\">\n  <h2>Computing, equipment and financial support</h2>\n  <p>Practical contributions may include suitable computing equipment, compute access, research hosting or support for a separately agreed independent review. These are additional ways to help alongside volunteer expertise.</p>\n  <details class=\"funding-details\"><summary>Equipment and paid-review planning estimates</summary><p>The 3 October 2026 planning brief proposed <strong>$6,500</strong> for a research laptop package and <strong>$4,000</strong> for a scoped independent mathematical review: <strong>$10,500</strong> total. These are preliminary US-dollar estimates, subject to quotations and agreed terms. Suitable in-kind resources reduce the corresponding cash need.</p><p>The computing baseline was 64 GB RAM and 2 TB storage; final configuration requires representative workload measurements and a dated quote. The small exact replay does not itself require a GPU.</p><p><a href=\"./source/funding/UD_RESEARCH_SUPPORT_BRIEF_v0.1.md\" download>Download the historical equipment and review brief</a>.</p></details>\n  <p>No payments are collected on this site. Financial, equipment and paid-review arrangements require agreed terms. No charitable status or tax-deductibility is represented; reviewer payment is for careful work regardless of conclusion.</p>\n</section>\n\n<section id=\"research-accountability\">\n  <h2>Contribution and research accountability</h2>\n  <p>UD is an independent program exploring geometric constraints and admissible dynamics on finite tetrahedral structures. Contributions should make a defined claim clearer, more reproducible or better tested. Supporting the project or reviewing one artifact does not confer endorsement of the whole framework.</p>\n  <p>Mathematical results, candidate physical correspondences and empirical evidence retain distinct status. Corrections and unfavorable findings remain in the research record. <strong>Physical promotion remains 0.</strong></p>\n</section>\n"
