    "sha256": "c61affe63a7ac2ab4ca0acaf28c41967c9e14a2c786968bd204d038d12c47fe5",
    "size_bytes": 7685,
    "content": "# UD packet-action event-source and renewal audit v0.1\n\n**12 October 2026 UTC. EXACT conditional two-branch kernel counterexample; NO-GO deriving a unique switch schedule from the available action/admissibility statements. OPEN native pair receipt, feedback/renewal and physical clock. Physical promotion 0.** This preserves the prior continuous contrast candidate as a candidate; no result is promoted to an autonomous UD law.\n\n## Source and status lock\n\nThe attached March 2026 `distinction_dynamics_manuscript.pdf` (SHA-256 `909ac4bfbb07ab815d15463648278877a7452989797589bf630564a0afa9f1ef`) is a **historical packet proposal**, not the current accepted event source. Its §§2,4 define packet variables `X_i=(rho_i,theta_i,chi_i)`, link transport `U_ij`, and a proposed action consisting of loop-holonomy, burden and orientation-mismatch terms. Its §13 gives an illustrative Monte Carlo loop: choose a random node or edge, propose a local `X_i` or `U_ij` change, compute `Delta S`, and accept with `min(1,exp(-Delta S/T))`. It does not specify a proposal distribution, all admissible moves, graph-update/renewal dynamics, a physical attempt clock, or a map from its local `chi_i` to the current K4 pair bits `Theta_p`. Those are separately typed.\n\nThe current [Paper I review draft v1.1.1 §7.4](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_I_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md) expressly leaves the pre-event binary offset/source outside its exact conditional map. The supplied `UD_COEFFICIENT_PROVENANCE_LEDGER_v0.39(2).md` (22 August 2026, SHA-256 `1281aa8454013fbbdbcf8ada07af0aefe81014003f25a27f3929ad43afffae63`) marks Q153's burden flux/source law as open, Q158's source/sink as a *residual receipt*, Q156/Q167/Q173's masks/currents as conditional on gates, and Q178/Q179's open-system renewal terms as unsourced. The [current UD portal](https://tetrahedral-packet-complexes.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/