    "content": "# UD cochain contrast clock and event-timing audit v0.1\n\n**12 October 2026 UTC. EXACT filled-K4 flow identity and sign-alias witness. NO-GO for deriving a unique event interval/trigger from present premises. The frozen cochain candidate remains a scoped discrete endpoint rule. Independent event test NOT_RUN; physical promotion 0.**\n\n## Source, version and typed question\n\n[Paper I review draft v1.1.1 §§4.1–4.2, 7.4](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_I_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md) defines the unit-weight oriented filled-K4 chain space, skew generator `A=d-d^T`, its fixed-chain flow `exp(sA)`, and leaves event receipt admission open. The supplied [coefficient ledger v0.39(2)](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/) (22 August 2026, SHA-256 `1281aa8454013fbbdbcf8ada07af0aefe81014003f25a27f3929ad43afffae63`, Q156/Q165–169/Q173) likewise separates the native generator from hard-mask factors and conditional currents. The [cochain contrast candidate v0.1 §§Typed objects–Verification](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-12T133647Z-codex-cochain-contrast-fc1f7596/PROTOCOL.md) freezes a *new* contrast-reversal trigger and Cayley step `h=1`, with no native source derivation. The [independent OP03 producer handoff v0.1 §Return checklist](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-11T020241Z-codex-op03-producer-handoff-23f7e091/PROVIDER_HANDOFF_v0.1.md) reports zero same-carrier independent full-endpoint submissions. No new endpoint corpus appears in the intervening candidate captures; no independent target is claimed here.\n\nQuestion: can the continuous native chain flow determine the candidate event interval and its discrete switch occurrence, and does the frozen endpoint sign rule resolve switch *times*? Chain amplitudes `c`, pairing bits `Theta`, contrast scores `d`, source receipts `xi`, local edge maps `U_e`, and physical time remain separately typed.\n\n## Exact K4 relation between the Cayley and native flows\n\nLet `P0` be orthogonal projection onto the uniform vertex vector, extended by zero to `C1⊕C2⊕C3`. Paper I §4.2 gives `A²=-4(I-P0)`, `AP0=P0A=0`. For real finite `h`, the rational Cayley map used in the frozen protocol is\n\n\\[\nQ_h=(I-\\tfrac h2A)^{-1}(I+\\tfrac h2A)\n=P_0+\\frac{1-h^2}{1+h^2}(I-P_0)+\\frac{h}{1+h^2}A.\n\\]\n\nThe exact native flow is\n\n\\[\ne^{sA}=P_0+\\cos(2s)(I-P_0)+\\frac{\\sin(2s)}2A.\n\\]\n\nWith `s=arctan(h)` on the principal branch, the double-angle identities give **`Q_h=exp(arctan(h) A)` for this filled K4**. Thus `Q_1=exp((π/4)A)=P0+A/2`, whereas `Q_(1/2)=exp(arctan(1/2) A)`. This exact equivalence corrects any impression that the frozen Cayley output is numerically approximate *on this carrier*. It does **not** identify `h=1` with native interval `s=1`, choose one internal interval over another, give a physical clock, extend the same one-frequency identity to glued A/B/C complexes, or derive a pair flip from continuous amplitudes. The exact Fraction checker constructs the signed boundary independently of the prior candidate implementation and verifies `A²`, the closed Cayley formula, orthogonality, and the defining Cayley equation at `h=1,1/2`.\n\n## Exact endpoint alias: net receipt does not identify switch times\n\nOn `C1`, `P0=0`; write `u=(c_0)_1` and `v=(A c_0)_1/2`. Then the native edge coordinates satisfy\n\n\\[\nc_1(s)=u\\cos(2s)+v\\sin(2s),\\qquad\nd_p(s)=\\alpha_p+\\beta_p\\cos(4s)+\\gamma_p\\sin(4s),\n\\]\n\nwhere `d_p=3 sum_{e∈p} c_{1,e}² - sum_{e}c_{1,e}²` and `α,β,γ` are exact quadratic expressions in the rational initial chain. This is a **constructed contrast proxy**, not the source-defined `G_p^{S±}` or a physical defect observable.\n\nUse the initial chain in the frozen 15-coordinate order\n\n`c0=(2,-2,2,1 | 2,2,0,0,-2,2 | 0,2,1,2 | 1)`.\n\nExact substitution gives the following three ordered contrasts:\n\n| Native parameter `s` | `d_A` | `d_B` | `d_C` |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| `0` | `8` | `8` | `-16` |\n| `π/8` | `-5/4` | `1` | `1/4` |\n| `π/4` | `43/2` | `-10` | `-23/2` |\n\nThe frozen **endpoint** rule therefore emits `xi=(0,1,0)`. Yet continuity forces at least **two distinct strict zeros** of `d_A` and at least two of `d_C` inside `(0,π/4)`, one on each side of `π/8`. They are uncounted by the endpoint reversal predicate. This is an **EXACT alias/no-go** only for identifying that predicate with *every continuous contrast-zero occurrence*. It does **not** contradict the frozen v0.1 definition, which expressly reports net endpoint sign reversals, and it is not evidence that real UD events occur at those mathematical zeros. A pre-event first-crossing dynamics would be a new, separately justified and frozen candidate.\n\nAn additional exact rational witness from the frozen protocol gives `xi=(1,0,0)` under `h=1` and `xi=(0,0,0)` under `h=1/2` at identical pre-state. Both steps are exact samples of the same native one-frequency flow, merely at different internal parameters. No symmetry, skewness or norm-preservation fact chooses one. The trigger itself remains an independent constitutive premise; merely finding an internal interval with simple algebra does not supply event admission.\n\n## Independent data gate and disposition\n\nNo independently produced same-carrier set with oriented pre-event cochains, complete ordered null/switch windows, frozen event clock, and hidden full `Theta` endpoints was available in the cited OP03 handoff or in the new v0.1 candidate capture. The `Gap2_FINAL_Finite_Genesis.png` attachment was unavailable. Accordingly the frozen candidate has **not** been tested against independent positive or null targets. The exact examples in `verify.py` are mathematical counterexamples/controls, not scored observations. Current physical promotion is **0**.\n\n**EXACT scoped:** the flow/Cayley identity on the unit-weight filled K4 and the two-interior-zero alias witness. **NO-GO scoped:** native skew flow and its symmetry do not select `h` or the contrast-trigger axiom; endpoint sign reversal is not an event-timing/count rule for all interior contrast zeros. **OPEN_GATED:** a sourced clock or first-passage/admission law; typed defect interpretation; local transport changes; independently produced same-carrier outcomes and all null windows; units, calibration, uncertainty and a preregistered physical acceptance rule. No revision of the frozen v0.1 candidate or its prior result file is made.\n"
