    "content": "# UD mathematics and theory closure assessment v0.1\n\n**11 October 2026 UTC.** Assessment, not a theorem or promotion receipt. Physical promotion: **0**. Constructor review only. The cited main-branch snapshot was commit `904d9902f60b121acb91e8036e837bff18aa3d9e`; subsequent changes require a new reconciliation.\n\n## Decision\n\n**OPEN — UD is not yet at “math and theory closed; only physical experiments remain.”** It has a substantial exact, reproducible *conditional* mathematical core. The laws determining which event occurs, when it occurs, and how some typed factors and open-system sources update are still not specified or uniquely selected. A conditional pushforward of a supplied event is not an autonomous prediction of that event.\n\nThere are two different possible closure targets:\n\n1. **Axiomatic model closure:** choose a complete, internally consistent dynamics on a declared carrier, prove its scoped properties, and freeze an observable/measurement dictionary and prospective predictions. Its axioms need not be uniquely forced by symmetry. After that, experimental correspondence can remain the open phase.\n2. **Unique physical unification:** derive the actual laws and constants of nature, quantum matter/gauge content, gravity and cosmology from UD primitives. Current evidence does not support this stronger closure; selecting plausible axioms does not establish it. Constants that are calibrated by future experiments must be declared as free parameters, not advertised as derived predictions.\n\n**Recommended target:** finish the first target, name its axiom choices and parameter degrees of freedom, and keep the second target OPEN. “Only experiments remain” applies to the *specified model and its declared tests*, not to every historical UD claim.\n\n## Current exact core and its boundary\n\n| Object / result | Supported status | Boundary of claim |\n|---|---|---|\n| Filled-tetrahedral chain carrier, incidence, S4 matching action, skew/Hodge flow; specified Pachner comparisons, spectra and period obstruction | **EXACT** for declared finite carriers and operators | Does not select a physical generator, metric, action scale, event source or clock. [Paper I v1.1.1 §§3–6, 9–10](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_I_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md). |\n| Given event receipt `(r,a)`, affine binary transition; given edge map, relative-frame extraction | **EXACT conditional** | Native derivation of `(r,a)` from the chain state remains OPEN; endpoint recovery is retrospective. [Paper I v1.1.1 §7.1–7.5](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_I_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md). |\n| Signed-stock/current reconstruction, parity ambiguity, forest/cycle identities, covariance map | **EXACT conditional** on support, sign/phase references and receipt assumptions | Acquiring the same physical coefficients, reference, uncertainty and time scale is a separate bridge. Complex recovery uses its separately specified receipt. [Paper II v1.1.1 §§2–9](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_II_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md). |\n| Shell recurrence, declared radial potential, spectral enclosures, relation algebra, finite controllers | **EXACT/CONDITIONAL** for supplied carriers/operators/controllers | Potential, beta, context response, renewal kernel and controller are choices; a prepared carrier is not a native formation law. Scalar probe visibility is narrower than spectral completeness. [Paper III v1.1.1 §§7–8, 12–16](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_III_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md). |\n| Matched SWAP correlation export and bounded finite-bank controller | **EXACT conditional** on supplied banks and joint-domain error contracts | Production, trigger, capture, reset, routing and sustained supply remain open; exact closed first-entry storage has a no-go under finite static Hermitian assumptions. [Paper III v1.1.1 §13](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_III_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md); [Paper IV v0.1 §§8–10](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_IV_REVIEW_DRAFT_v0.1.md). |\n| Edge hard mask `h_e=C_e T_e` and direct-Theta event-to-closure lift | **EXACT conditional** on typed factors or externally supplied flip receipt `xi` | Neither factor transition, edge transport update nor pre-event cause of `xi` is supplied. The particular pair-lift closure factor is not every context's closure predicate. [Source-readiness report v0.1 §§Result–Pre-event candidate](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-10T163105Z-codex-source-readiness-3c72f65b/REPORT.md); [Theta pushforward v0.1 §§Source recovery–Endogenous source](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-10T170752Z-codex-theta-closure-245626d6/REPORT.md). |\n\nThe supplied local `UD_COEFFICIENT_PROVENANCE_LEDGER_v0.39(2).md` (22 August 2026, SHA-256 `1281aa8454013fbbdbcf8ada07af0aefe81014003f25a27f3929ad43afffae63`, entries G05/G06/Q139/Q143/Q152/Q153 and B/H) is a dated baseline retaining distinct open or quarantined physical coefficients and constitutive laws. The supplied `Gap2_FINAL_STATUS.md` (SHA-256 `436c87fbe121d3a9a845d356d786ab299e83a6dd84285698acc92c8f3a1a514a`, §§Conclusions–Caveats) makes more optimistic cosmological statements but itself leaves direct spectrum and free parameters open. Later ledger/paper authority prevents using the older statements as current parameter-free physical results. This is a **version conflict in claim scope**, not a mathematical refutation of every older computation. The attached governance subdivision v1.0 is a proposal, not a completed independent-review rung.\n\n## Theory-side gaps, ordered by dependency\n\n| Gate | Missing definition or proof | Why physical experiments cannot close it on their own | Exit evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **G1. Autonomous event source and admissibility** | State space including memory and lineage; native source/renewal rule; event/no-event interval; collision and tie rule; address/frame and affine toggle; initial/boundary conditions; deterministic or stochastic semantics. | Given the same reduced pre-state, multiple admitted event receipts remain possible. If a stochastic rule is chosen, its probability kernel and filtration must be fixed before outcomes. | Versioned generator `F` or Markov kernel on typed complete pre-state, null windows included; existence/uniqueness or well-posedness, symmetry, conserved/budget quantities, exact counterexamples, and target-blind endpoint predictions. [Paper I §7.4, §8.4](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_I_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md); [OP03 handoff v0.1](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-11T020241Z-codex-op03-producer-handoff-23f7e091/PROVIDER_HANDOFF_v0.1.md). |\n| **G2. Typed mask and source law** | `F_E:(x_pre,e_pre)->(C'_e,T'_e)` with independently sourced local edge maps, requirements, overlap/reverse tests; separate pair-gate response `G` and, if claimed, pair-to-edge intertwiner. | `h_e=C_eT_e` calculates a mask from factors; it does not predict next factors. Pair-only equivariance outputs at most eight pair-constant masks of the 64 possible six-edge binary masks. The scope is representation capacity, not physical occurrence of all 64. | Sourced edge-resolved variables or explicitly restricted mask family; exact equivariance and boundary proof; independent endpoints for nontrivial switch and intact-null close/hold. [Pair-edge obstruction v0.1](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-10T161720Z-codex-pair-edge-22aece15/REPORT.md); [source-readiness v0.1](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-10T163105Z-codex-source-readiness-3c72f65b/REPORT.md). |\n| **G3. Multicell open-system dynamics** | Contact activation/admission, lawful polarity, ordering of shared-copy contacts, source/sink and constitutive edge flux, renewal resources and complete-joint controller trigger. | Finite algebra proves conditional conservation/transport, while lawful simultaneous evolution depends on these inputs. Symmetric exclusive selection has a no-go without added record/symmetry break; shared contacts need not commute. | One owned joint domain with complete generator and schedule, conservation/balance, well-posed global/finite-horizon theorem, all failure and resource branches. [Paper I §§8.2–8.4](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_I_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md); [Paper IV §§8–10](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_IV_REVIEW_DRAFT_v0.1.md); supplied ledger v0.39 Q153/Q157/Q160, SHA-256 above. |\n| **G4. Coarse/continuum/action map** | Explicit scaling limit or error-controlled coarse map from discrete state and operator to metric/clock/action/energy and local fields; identify observables, dimensions, signs, normalization and boundary data. | Equal numerical values or arbitrary rescaling cannot identify typed micro and macro objects. Current geometry/second moments do not identify `omega_E`; `K_facecomp` is not `sigma_C` by default. | Proved projectability/limit or quantified approximation; independent invariant checks, nonunique-map counterexamples addressed; declared free scales and parameter sensitivity. [Paper I §9](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_I_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md); supplied ledger v0.39 G05/Q139/Q143, SHA-256 above. |\n| **G5. Physical claim scope and prediction specification** | Which sector actually claims gravity, matter/gauge, quantum behavior or cosmology; which coefficients are derived versus fitted; observable, unit, baseline, uncertainty, acceptance and falsifier. | Experiments cannot test an undefined or target-adjusted prediction; they can estimate declared free parameters only under a frozen calibration protocol. | One versioned claim ledger and manuscripts; freeze or retract unsupported full-unification/hierarchy/cosmology claims; preregister target-blind bridge tests and independent validation. [Paper I §9](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_I_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md); [Paper II §9](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_II_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md); [Paper III §14](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_III_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md). |\n\n### Critical counterexamples and scope constraints\n\n- **NO-GO under reduced inputs:** `Theta+ = P_g Theta- XOR xi` is exact for a sourced `xi`, but the same `Theta-`, frame and fixed transport factors permit distinct post-states when different valid external receipts are supplied. This does not rule out a richer native law. [Theta pushforward v0.1 §Endogenous source](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-10T170752Z-codex-theta-closure-245626d6/REPORT.md).\n- **NO-GO under pair-only state and full S4 covariance:** the kernel `V4` fixes each pair bit and exchanges its two edges, forcing pair-constant output; 56 of 64 algebraic edge masks are outside that image. This does not assert those 56 occur physically. [Pair-edge obstruction v0.1 §Exact symmetry obstruction](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-10T161720Z-codex-pair-edge-22aece15/REPORT.md).\n- **NO-GO under symmetric exclusive progress:** an automorphism exchanging two equally eligible contacts cannot select exactly one covariantly and deterministically while always progressing. Add a record, stochasticity, batch rule or source asymmetry, then prove the new branch. [Paper I v1.1.1 §8.4](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-07T191951Z-codex-ud-bootstrap-5170f8b8/browse/dist/papers/UD_PAPER_I_REVIEW_DRAFT_v1.1.1.md).\n- **OPEN/UNSCORED:** OP03's v0.2.1 conditional guard passes bounded finite cases, and its frame-alignment audit identifies 144 caller-misuse event labels among 1,296 admitted cases. No independent full-endpoint target was supplied; target-generated history is ineligible for a blind selector score. [OP03 handoff v0.1 §Return checklist](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-11T020241Z-codex-op03-producer-handoff-23f7e091/PROVIDER_HANDOFF_v0.1.md); [alignment audit v0.1 §Exact finite audit](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-11-codex-op03-frame-alignment-v01/OP03_FRAME_ALIGNMENT_VALIDATOR_NOTE_v0.1.md); [eligibility audit v0.1](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/captures/2026-10-10T165456Z-codex-event-eligibility-d4d33a75/REPORT.md).\n\n## Closure acceptance rule\n\nMark **MATH/THEORY CLOSED (scoped model only)** only when: (a) a canonical versioned axiom list defines typed carriers, full state, initial/boundary data, generator or kernel, source/admission/mask rules and readout on one compatible domain; (b) claimed global or finite-horizon dynamics, conservation/budget, covariance, support, limits and known no-go forks have proof or reproducible exact certificates, with independent reimplementation of central identities; (c) free coefficients and constitutive choices are labeled, identifiability is stated, and legacy incompatible claims are frozen/amended; (d) a measurement dictionary and prospective, target-blind predictions, calibration-only parameters, uncertainties, null models and falsifiers are frozen. An unresolved mathematical existence, selection or consistency premise fails the gate. Independent review is a separate required evidence gate, not a physical experiment.\n\n**Prioritized path:** P1 close G1/G2 on a bounded, complete K4 pair-and-edge model including null windows and a pre-event source; seek countermodels first. P2 join G3 to that model and prove joint-domain evolution/resource bounds. P3 derive or explicitly stipulate G4 with dimensions and projection error, then freeze G5. P4 independent proof/code review and prospective preregistration. Only then run the physical bridge experiments; their outcome may falsify the model. A narrow axiomatic model can meet this gate while the stronger universal-derivation claim remains open.\n\n**Limitations:** This is a source-bound synthesis, not a fresh theorem or exhaustive audit of every later archive file. The missing local `Gap2_FINAL_Finite_Genesis.png` was not inspected. No fresh mathematical replay, independent review, held-out source event or physical experiment is claimed.\n"
