    "content": "# Theorem — \\(\\Delta^4\\) Discrete 3-Form Gauge Prototype v0.1\n\n**Status:** `EXACT FINITE COCHAIN THEOREM / CANDIDATE GAUGE-FACING LANE`  \n**Physical promotion:** `0`\n\nLet\n\n\\[\nC^k(\\Delta^4)=\\operatorname{Hom}(C_k(\\Delta^4),\\mathbb R)\n\\]\n\nwith canonical oriented simplex bases and coboundaries\n\n\\[\n\\delta_k=B_{k+1}^{\\mathsf T}.\n\\]\n\nDefine a degree-three cochain\n\n\\[\nA_3\\in C^3(\\Delta^4)\n\\]\n\nand its degree-four curvature cochain\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nF_4=\\delta_3A_3.\n}\n\\]\n\nFor any\n\n\\[\n\\Lambda_2\\in C^2(\\Delta^4),\n\\]\n\ndefine the finite gauge transformation\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nA_3\\mapsto A_3+\\delta_2\\Lambda_2.\n}\n\\]\n\nBecause\n\n\\[\n\\delta_3\\delta_2\n=\n(B_3B_4)^{\\mathsf T}\n=\n0,\n\\]\n\nthe curvature is exactly invariant:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nF_4\\mapsto F_4.\n}\n\\]\n\nOn \\(\\Delta^4\\),\n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{rank}\\delta_2=4,\n\\qquad\n\\operatorname{rank}\\delta_3=1.\n\\]\n\nSince \\(H^3(\\Delta^4)=0\\),\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\ker\\delta_3=\\operatorname{im}\\delta_2.\n}\n\\]\n\nTherefore\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nC^3/\\operatorname{im}\\delta_2\n\\cong\nC^4\n}\n\\]\n\nthrough the induced map \\(\\delta_3\\). The complete gauge-invariant content of one global 3-cochain on a single 4-simplex is exactly one scalar top-cochain coordinate \\(F_4\\).\n\nUnder the declared orthonormal simplex-basis pairing,\n\n\\[\nB_4^{\\mathsf T}B_4=5.\n\\]\n\nHence every gauge orbit has the unique minimum-norm representative\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nA_3^\\perp\n=\n\\frac{F_4}{5}B_4.\n}\n\\]\n\nNo M-theory, spacetime, brane, or physical gauge identity follows from this theorem.\n"
