    "content": "# UD_GENESIS_HODGE_CANONICAL_ACTION_CLOCK_INTERTWINER_v0.1\n\n**Date:** 2026-09-13  \n**Purpose:** return from the historical cluster lane to the highest-leverage action/clock bridge and derive the strongest target-blind Genesis↔Hodge canonical relation currently supported  \n**Status:** `EXACT_LOCAL_CANONICAL_REDUCTION__CONDITIONAL_SAME-HISTORY_INTERTWINER__GLOBAL_NONSTATIONARY_CLOCK_NO-GO`  \n**Physical promotion:** `0`\n\n# 1. Source objects and typing\n\nHistorical Genesis supplies:\n\n\\[\n\\hbar_d\n\\]\n\nas a **postulated distinction-event action quantum**,\n\n\\[\n\\tau_d\n\\]\n\nas the historical fundamental time parameter,\n\n\\[\n\\Delta a_{\\rm G}\n\\]\n\nas the amplitude increment per distinction event, and the slow-genesis kinetic action\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nS_{\\rm G,kin}\n=\n\\frac{K_G}{2}\n\\int \\dot a^2\\,dt\n}\n\\]\n\nfor one local mode, with\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nK_G\n:=\n\\frac{\\hbar_d\\tau_d}{\\Delta a_{\\rm G}^2}.\n}\n\\]\n\nThe source-stratum dimensional normalization states\n\n\\[\n\\Delta a_{\\rm G}^2=\\hbar_d\\tau_d,\n\\]\n\nhence \\(K_G=1\\) in that historical normalization. This relation is retained symbolically until the final reduction.\n\nCurrent Hodge canon separately supplies\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\Omega_{\\rm H}\n=\n\\mathcal A_0\\,dq\\wedge dp_H\n}\n\\]\n\non one active complex plane and\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\frac{d\\widetilde\\phi}{dt}\n=\n\\frac{2}{\\tau_0}\n}\n\\]\n\nunder the native physical-time dimensionalization \\(t=\\tau_0 s\\).\n\nHistorical \\(\\hbar_d\\) is **not** identified with physical \\(\\hbar\\).\n\nCurrent \\(\\mathcal A_0\\) is **not** identified with \\(2\\hbar\\).\n\nPhysical promotion remains zero.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Local historical harmonic carrier\n\nOn a locally stationary Genesis background, let the active node mode satisfy\n\n\\[\n\\frac{d^2a}{du^2}\n+\n\\omega_G^2a\n=\n0,\n\\]\n\nwhere\n\n\\[\nu:=t/\\tau_d\n\\]\n\nand \\(\\omega_G\\) is dimensionless.\n\nThus the dimensional historical angular frequency is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\omega_{\\rm G}^{\\rm phys}\n=\n\\frac{\\omega_G}{\\tau_d}.\n}\n\\]\n\nDefine the balanced historical phase coordinate\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\np_G\n:=\n\\frac{\\dot a}{\\omega_{\\rm G}^{\\rm phys}}.\n}\n\\]\n\nThen a harmonic orbit has\n\n\\[\na=A\\cos\\theta,\n\\qquad\np_G=-A\\sin\\theta,\n\\]\n\nand therefore\n\n\\[\na^2+p_G^2=A^2.\n\\]\n\n---\n\n# 3. Historical canonical symplectic form\n\nThe historical canonical momentum is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\pi_a\n=\n\\frac{\\partial L_G}{\\partial\\dot a}\n=\nK_G\\dot a\n=\nK_G\\omega_{\\rm G}^{\\rm phys}p_G.\n}\n\\]\n\nHence\n\n\\[\nd\\pi_a\n=\nK_G\\omega_{\\rm G}^{\\rm phys}\\,dp_G\n\\]\n\nfor a locally stationary carrier.\n\nThe historical symplectic form is therefore\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\Omega_G\n=\nda\\wedge d\\pi_a\n=\nK_G\\omega_{\\rm G}^{\\rm phys}\n\\,da\\wedge dp_G.\n}\n\\]\n\nOrientation reversal changes an overall sign only. The action scale uses the positive orientation magnitude.\n\n---\n\n# 4. GH-1 balanced coordinate map\n\nThe already-derived source-typed GH-1 node map fixes the configuration shape up to one normalization:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nq=c\\,a.\n}\n\\]\n\nFor a dynamical intertwiner of equal local frequency, the balanced companion must scale identically up to orientation:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\np_H\n=\n\\epsilon c\\,p_G,\n\\qquad\n\\epsilon\\in\\{+1,-1\\}.\n}\n\\]\n\nThus\n\n\\[\ndq\\wedge dp_H\n=\n\\epsilon c^2\n\\,da\\wedge dp_G.\n\\]\n\nIgnoring the orientation sign in the positive action scale,\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nda\\wedge dp_G\n=\n\\frac1{c^2}\ndq\\wedge dp_H.\n}\n\\]\n\nSubstitution into the historical symplectic form gives\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\Omega_G\n=\n\\frac{\nK_G\\omega_{\\rm G}^{\\rm phys}\n}{\nc^2\n}\ndq\\wedge dp_H.\n}\n\\]\n\n---\n\n# 5. Conditional canonical identity theorem\n\nIf the source-typed GH-1 carrier is admitted as the **same local canonical history** as the current Hodge active plane, then\n\n\\[\n\\Omega_G=\\Omega_H.\n\\]\n\nTherefore\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\mathcal A_0\n=\n\\frac{\nK_G\\omega_{\\rm G}^{\\rm phys}\n}{\nc^2\n}.\n}\n\\]\n\nUsing\n\n\\[\nK_G\n=\n\\frac{\\hbar_d\\tau_d}{\\Delta a_{\\rm G}^2}\n\\]\n\nand\n\n\\[\n\\omega_{\\rm G}^{\\rm phys}\n=\n\\frac{\\omega_G}{\\tau_d},\n\\]\n\nobtain the exact conditional action relation\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\mathcal A_0\n=\n\\frac{\n\\hbar_d\\omega_G\n}{\nc^2\\Delta a_{\\rm G}^2\n}.\n}\n\\]\n\nHence\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\frac{\\mathcal A_0}{\\hbar_d}\n=\n\\frac{\n\\omega_G\n}{\nc^2\\Delta a_{\\rm G}^2\n}.\n}\n\\]\n\nThis uses no physical \\(\\hbar\\), no Newton \\(G\\), and no target action value.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Elimination by the active event length\n\nThe exact GH-2 event geometry gives\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\delta_H^2\n=\n\\frac34\nc^2\\Delta a_{\\rm G}^2.\n}\n\\]\n\nTherefore\n\n\\[\nc^2\\Delta a_{\\rm G}^2\n=\n\\frac43\\delta_H^2.\n\\]\n\nThe action ratio becomes\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\frac{\\mathcal A_0}{\\hbar_d}\n=\n\\frac{\n3\\omega_G\n}{\n4\\delta_H^2\n}.\n}\n\\]\n\nThis is a stronger result than the earlier separate amplitude gauge statement.\n\nThe historical primitive amplitude increment and cross-lineage scale \\(c\\) enter only through the gauge-invariant current-Hodge event length \\(\\delta_H\\).\n\n---\n\n# 7. Clock intertwiner\n\nCurrent Hodge local phase rate is\n\n\\[\n\\omega_{\\rm H}^{\\rm phys}\n=\n\\frac2{\\tau_0}.\n\\]\n\nSame local dynamical history requires\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\omega_G}{\\tau_d}\n=\n\\frac2{\\tau_0}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\frac{\\tau_0}{\\tau_d}\n=\n\\frac2{\\omega_G}.\n}\n\\]\n\nEquivalently,\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\tau_0\n=\n\\frac{2\\tau_d}{\\omega_G}.\n}\n\\]\n\nNo absolute seconds are obtained.\n\nThis is a ratio theorem only.\n\n---\n\n# 8. Action-clock product invariant\n\nMultiply the action and clock ratios:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\mathcal A_0}{\\hbar_d}\n\\frac{\\tau_0}{\\tau_d}\n=\n\\frac{3\\omega_G}{4\\delta_H^2}\n\\frac2{\\omega_G}.\n\\]\n\nThe local frequency cancels exactly:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\frac{\n\\mathcal A_0\\tau_0\n}{\n