nIts positive oriented magnitude is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n|\\mathscr J_G|\n=\n\\pi\nK_G\\omega_{\\rm G}^{\\rm phys}\nA^2.\n}\n\\]\n\nUnder\n\n\\[\nq=c\\,a,\n\\qquad\np_H=\\epsilon c\\,p_G,\n\\]\n\nthe Hodge orbit radius is\n\n\\[\na_H\n=\nq^2+p_H^2\n=\nc^2A^2.\n\\]\n\nThe current Hodge recurrence action is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nS_{\\rm H,rec}\n=\n\\pi\\mathcal A_0a_H.\n}\n\\]\n\nUsing the canonical identity theorem,\n\n\\[\n\\mathcal A_0\n=\n\\frac{\nK_G\\omega_{\\rm G}^{\\rm phys}\n}{\nc^2\n},\n\\]\n\ngives\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\nS_{\\rm H,rec}\n=\n|\\mathscr J_G|.\n}\n\\]\n\nThis is not assumed by matching two action formulas.\n\nIt follows from equality of the local symplectic form.\n\n### Scoped promotion\n\n`GENESIS_HARMONIC_ACTION_VARIABLE_EQUALS_HODGE_RECURRENCE_AREA_THEOREM_v0.1`\n\nis AUTO_LOCKED as **EXACT CONDITIONAL** on the same-history canonical intertwiner.\n\nIt is not a proof that the historical Genesis action equals the current packet master action globally.\n\n---\n\n# 12. Global nonstationary clock no-go\n\nThe current Hodge carrier has fixed native phase rate\n\n\\[\n2/\\tau_0.\n\\]\n\nThe historical local frequency is generally sourced by state-dependent Genesis variables such as\n\n\\[\n\\Omega,\\quad\n\\Phi,\\quad\n\\kappa_{\\rm eff},\n\\]\n\nand nonlinear amplitude corrections.\n\nIf\n\n\\[\n\\omega_G=\\omega_G(t)\n\\]\n\nvaries along a Genesis history, then same-time local matching would require\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\tau_0}{\\tau_d}\n=\n\\frac{2}{\\omega_G(t)}.\n\\]\n\nA single constant ratio \\(\\tau_0/\\tau_d\\) cannot satisfy this for all \\(t\\) unless\n\n\\[\n\\omega_G(t)=\\text{constant}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\text{nonstationary Genesis history}\n\\not\\Rightarrow\n\\text{one global constant Genesis↔Hodge clock identification}.\n}\n\\]\n\n### AUTO_LOCK NO-GO\n\nA global clock bridge requires one of:\n\n1. a source-derived stationary/equilibrium Genesis carrier;\n2. a dynamically varying Hodge clock law supplied by a new source amendment