    "content": "# UD presentation claim and source reconciliation v0.2\n\n14 October 2026 UTC. Development / presentation amendment; no scientific registry promotion. Physical promotion 0.\n\nAll 448 current ledger rows have a source-row copy, reuse disposition, historical comparison, explicit textual references and amendment links. The 235-row v0.39 ledger and later v0.65 original are preserved separately. This is a source/status audit, not a reproof of all rows. Textual citations are not asserted to be causal proof dependencies: the complete proof DAG remains OPEN_GATED.\n\n{\n  \"edition\": \"0.2\",\n  \"date\": \"2026-10-14\",\n  \"rows_reviewed\": 448,\n  \"historical_rows\": 235,\n  \"new_rows\": 213,\n  \"unchanged_rows\": 229,\n  \"changed_rows\": 6,\n  \"amendments\": 10,\n  \"rows_with_amendments\": 91,\n  \"explicit_reference_occurrences\": 32,\n  \"all_rows_have_source_and_reuse_limit\": true,\n  \"proof_dependency_DAG\": \"OPEN_GATED\",\n  \"full_reproof\": \"NOT_PERFORMED\",\n  \"physical_promotion\": 0\n}\n\n## Versioned dispositions\n\n### ARA01 — Retired universal scalar action\n\nThe current ledger retires a universal kappa_loop scalar. Conditional scalar-family algebra survives only on its declared domain. A native action form or numerical internal ratio does not fix a dimensional physical action, clock or gravity scale.\n\nScope: No retraction of a proved formula conditional on a supplied scalar; unqualified mainline/physical reuse is held.\n\nSources: L65, E07, PIV, E11; G05, G06, O09 and Q139; Paper IV §9; clock theorem §§2–9\n\n### ARA02 — Receipt index needs idle-response correction\n\nOn the admitted pair-response domain, mu_Theta = ind F_omega + |h^-| - |h^+| with h=q-omega, after frame alignment. The index alone is full polarity only if the idle term vanishes. Binding POC-1 saturation fixes the response address; a nontrivial competing burden optimizer is then not a simultaneous final selector.\n\nScope: Retains conditional index identities