arrier. Fixed K does not select spatial refinement. The strict contract of native contraction, unit singleton readout and unweighted-generator intertwining fails on K4 to sd K4 because 7>3.\n\nScope: An indefinite internal form, finite event mediator and physical spacetime metric are distinct. Q107 lists counts through degree 3; a full filled 4-simplex also has one 4-cell.\n\nSources: R29, R30, R33, R34, G14, E09, E10, A06; Lorentzian gate §§2–5; native refinement §3; interface gate §2; governance §7\n\n### ARA07 — Receipt memory timing and physical resource scale\n\nThe decomposed write has 34 slots. A 44-slot total deadline leaves 10 storage rounds; 32 post-write rounds require 66 total slots. Gibbs flag probabilities and normalized accuracy do not identify joules, physical area or a fully renewed controller/bath cycle.\n\nScope: Retains fixed-age calculations with their original schedule. No entropy/horizon normalization is backsolved from Newton G.\n\nSources: R36, R40, PIV, E11; Entropy session summary; receipt gap frontier clock and non-identifiability; Paper IV §9\n\n### ARA08 — Historical Gap 2 sign and parameter audit\n\nFor n_s<1, 0<rho<1 and contraction 0<r<1, the displayed -(n_s-1)|ln rho|/ln(1/r) is positive. It cannot equal the reported negative running under those assumptions. Its dependence on n_s also inherits the unresolved n_CMB unless a separate source or conditional measured-pivot forecast is declared.\n\nScope: A new presentation audit, not a silent correction of the original formula. Recover the scale convention and original derivation/code before selecting a repaired sign or claiming a parameter-free prediction.\n\nSources: A14, A06, L65; Gap2_FINAL_STATUS.md §6, equations A.6 and A.19; historical fits\n\n### ARA09 — Replay counts and review types\n\nThe edge-receipt count 1551 denotes selected manually counted check groups, not all assertions; the later AST instrumentation reports 1837 evaluated assertions. Gemini replication and separate AI