    "content": "# UD minimal pre-event response source theorem v0.1\n\n14 October 2026 UTC. Development — no registry entry. Constructor: Codex.\nStatus: EXACT CONDITIONAL FINITE ALGEBRA / NATIVE SOURCE OPEN. Physical promotion: 0.\nIndependent adversarial proof review of this new result remains pending.\n\n## 1. Source and domain\n\nSource anchors: C0963, `declared_source_variables`, `exact_response_form`, `minimum_missing_object`; C0957, theorem and saturated-prior corollary; C0884 §§2, 7, 9; October 13 synthetic polarity audit E04 §§2–5. These source-text snapshots are preserved in the v0.3 dependency register with hashes. The attached v0.39 ledger, Q165–Q173, supplies fixed-carrier support and flux, not a response source law. The attached governance CRL-2 subdivision v1.0 is a proposal; its development lane and promotion distinctions are retained. None of these imported labels establishes independent review.\n\nOn three pair addresses fix binary prospective integrity T and latent-presence L, constructed independently before endpoint exposure. Define omega=T AND L and I=T AND NOT L. A response q=1−Theta is admitted iff omega≤q≤T coordinatewise. I is the intact-null potential mask; h is the actual idle-open response mask. They are not the same object. Prospective T and L are source outputs from a frozen pre-event mechanism, not retrospectively inferred post-event measurements.\n\n## 2. Exact response-fiber theorem\n\nEvery admitted q has a unique representation q=omega+h with binary h≤I. Conversely every such h yields an admitted q. Proof: omega≤q makes h=q−omega nonnegative; q≤T restricts h to T=1,L=0; omega and h have disjoint support. The reverse follows coordinatewise.\n\nWrite i=|I|. The response fiber has exactly 2^i masks. With independently sourced idle count j, its cardinality is binomial(i,j), 0≤j≤i. For i=0,1,2,3 the full cardinalities are 1,2,4,8. There are 64 possible (T,L) pairs. Their i histogram is (27,27,9,1), by (3+x)^3. The sum of response fiber