d tie-break can break this stabilizer, but must be separately sourced. This theorem does not cover a selector using that additional information.\n\nA stochastic kernel invariant under the same intact-null stabilizer has one probability p_j per cardinality orbit j=0,...,i. Every individual mask of size j has probability p_j/binomial(i,j); p_j≥0 and sum p_j=1. Conversely these formulas define every invariant kernel. There are i unconstrained probability degrees of freedom. Symmetry alone does not determine them or native clock rates. Conditioning on a supplied j gives a uniform invariant distribution on that orbit; it does not derive which j occurs.\n\n## 5. Pre-event source contract\n\nA complete prospective packet must declare: complete pre-state and its update index; old Theta,T,L; old-to-current frame permutation and source receipt; prospective output T,L generated from that pre-state; actual h or the count j with declared address policy; the frozen source construction, version/hash, event/null behavior, collision/tie behavior, feedback and renewal semantics; input seal, prediction freeze and endpoint-release chronology. Prior Theta and omega must both be transported before directed-address readout.\n\nNet-budget-only admission can omit h addresses if it independently sources j. It cannot then claim a unique directed address except when binomial(i,j)=1. Full lineage provenance still additionally needs continuation/predecessor, merger and source/renewal records. A finite index difference does not supply these records.\n\nThe included reference receipt validator covers the full-mask route. It checks bits, prior admissibility, permutation convention, residual support, source-artifact SHA-256, binding of receipt fields, ordinal index and declared custody chronology. It rejects endpoint exposure, inconsistent source bytes and missing native program declarations. It does not execute a native law, authenticate timestamps, prove causal independence, establish artifact truth or certify empirical scoring eligibility. A structurally complete native-candidate packet still returns NATIVE_VALIDATION_PENDING__NO_SCORE.\n\nNo supplied specimen is native data. The example is explicitly synthetic: a declared pre-event construction supplies all masks and a candidate h=0. Another lawful h can give a different output on the same reduced variables. This tests the conditional readout, not model selection or a frozen POC-1 sidecar.\n\n## 6. What closes and what remains open\n\nClosed in the development lane: finite response parameterization, exact ambiguity/cardinality, count-versus-address distinction and restricted symmetry classification. The source obligation is reduced to independently deriving prospective T,L and an idle-response law/kernel on I, plus the frame and event/null chronology.\n\nOPEN: native viability generation; native idle-response selection or probability weights; full pre-state and renewal law; native frame receipt; source-authenticated timing/custody; independent adversarial review; lawful target-hidden physical episode and scorer custody. Physical promotion: 0. The original primary sidecar and its missing-byte boundary are unchanged.\n\nThe user's “reviewed; continue next steps” acknowledges the prior presentation. It is not recorded as a theorem-specific adversarial finding, custodial promotion or independent empirical result. No original scientific registry status is changed.\n"
