    "content": "# UD RSP-1 finite pre-event source programme v0.1\n\n14 October 2026 UTC. Development — no registry entry. Physical promotion: 0.\nStatus: CANDIDATE SOURCE-INTERFACE COMPLETION / EXACT CONDITIONAL FINITE RESULTS.\nConstructor team: Codex root and parallel mathematical design thread. Separate AI source/scope audit recorded; independent human/adversarial review and physical correspondence remain pending.\n\n## 1. Source audit and purpose\n\nThe v0.1 response contract isolated the missing prospective T,L,h source. C0593, Close-vs-Hold theorem and manuscript addendum, already supplies two lawful maps on given inputs: C(q−,T+,L+)=T+L+ and H(q−,T+,L+)=T+(q− OR T+L+). They are local, equivariant, idempotent under fixed source inputs and commute across addresses. They differ at intact latent extinction. Neither is selected natively. The frozen historical sidecar is not changed by this programme.\n\nRSP-1 now supplies a complete deterministic recurrence on an explicitly prepared finite register carrier and runs BOTH response maps on that carrier. It is a new candidate model, not recovery of a missing original native equation. Its source outputs precede its computed response; no target endpoint, target polarity, physical constant or fitted threshold enters the recurrence.\n\nExact source anchors: C0593, Close-vs-Hold theorem; C0926 §4.6, latent witness and pair-integrity readout; C0635 §9, edge integrity; C0621 §3, exact-zero instantaneous-rate no-go; E01, general deterministic factorization; E03, complete-state/visible-closure criterion; RESPONSE01 §§2–5, idle domain and pre-event contract. The attached v0.39 ledger Q153/Q158/Q165–Q173/Q178–Q179 and governance proposal retain their original limits.\n\n## 2. Complete prepared state and typed choices\n\nLet X=(T,L_cache,q,r,B,k,beta). T,L_cache,q are three-bit masks, T L_cache≤q≤T. L_cache records the previously completed latent-presence receipt; it is NOT recomputed from current stock while reading the old state. r is a nonnegative integer three-vector of prepared tokens. B=(b^(1),...,b^(B)) is a finite ordered queue of similarly prepared token tuples; k is its cursor. All current and bank stock is supported on T. beta=C or H is frozen for the episode. T is held fixed; the labeled pair frame is the identity. The observer's ordinal index is receipt metadata, excluded from the dynamical fixed-point test.\n\nFor each fixed preparation, stock components are bounded by the maximum initially supplied component, the cursor by B, and all response/cache variables are binary. The dynamical carrier is finite. No unspecified continuous variable is needed to compute its next state. Invalid initial masks, negative stock, stock on broken-integrity addresses, invalid cursor or unknown branch are rejected as invalid model input, not physical no-event.\n\nThese are supplied CANDIDATE choices: counter carrier and preparation, fixed-integrity law T+=T, identity frame, demand/feedback rule, unit consumption, bank-loading policy, branch and ordinal attempt convention. The source-complete recurrence resolves conditional model specification; it does not prove these choices are native UD dynamics.\n\n## 3. Total update and chronology\n\nFirst test whether r=q=L_cache=000 and k<B. If so, a RENEWAL_ONLY tick loads r+=b^(k+1), advances k, and leaves q+=L_cache+=000. Zero bank tuples still advance the cursor. That packet is inspected on the next tick. This is a finite preloaded supply, not generation of fresh resources.\n\nOtherwise perform an INSPECTION:\n\nR_p^(RSP)=r_p(1−q_p),\nL_p+=T_p 1[r_p>0](1−q_p),\nomega_p+=T_p L_p+,\nr_p+=r_p−omega_p+.\n\nThis is an explicitly chosen demand-inhibited positive-stock source. An already open response suppresses a new viable pulse; stock remains available until a later permitted pulse. Every address is processed simultaneously. The fixed-integrity copy and positive-stock source produce prospective T+,L+ before the response map is applied.\n\nC branch: h+=000, q+=omega+.\n\nH branch: I+=T(1−L+), h+=I+ q, q+=omega+ OR(T q).\n\nThe hold mask is recomputed on CURRENT I+. Blindly carrying old h can violate admission when viability changes. Both branches obey omega+≤q+≤T. Store the new cache L+ and response q+ and commit every full-state change, including RESPONSE_NULL ticks with unchanged q. Theta+=1−q+ and the directed toggle masks follow from the existing response-contract algebra.\n\nThe demand-inhibition feedback, consumption and renewal maps are part of the candidate definition. They are not consequences of the source C/H regularity theorem. That theorem's idempotence assumes fixed T,L inputs; the complete RSP recurrence changes its source registers and must be checked separately.\n\n## 4. Events, null updates and stopping\n\nTag BIT_EVENT iff the gross directed toggle count is nonzero. The full Hamming budget is muTheta=|q−|−|q+|; muTheta=0 can still be a mixed-address bit event. RESPONSE_NULL means unchanged pair response. It does NOT mean unchanged source state, absent source inspection or physical no-event.\n\nUse muTheta=ind Fomega+|h−|−|h+| with old omega=T L_cache. All masks are already in the fixed declared frame. On a future moving-frame extension every addressed register and old receipt must be transported together; that extension is not supplied here.\n\nStop only when the complete successor X+ equals X, including cached L, stock and cursor. HALT is a programme control result. Report EXHAUSTED_QUIESCENT only if all current and unspent stock is zero, cursor is at the end and q=L_cache=000. Otherwise report LATCHED_OR_STRANDED. A model fixed point is not an empirical physical no-event verdict or a calibrated waiting-time law.\n\n## 5. Exact conditional stock and termination theorem\n\nDefine S(X)=|r|+sum_{j>k}|b^(j)|. Renewal preserves S; inspection reduces it by |omega+|. Therefore S is nonincreasing. A response closure can occur without consuming a token; resource exhaustion cannot be inferred from a toggle alone.\n\nDefine the integer potential\n\nV(X)=4S(X)+2|q|+|L_cache|+(B−k).\n\nEvery committed tick strictly decreases V for BOTH branches. On renewal, S and masks are unchanged and B−k falls by one. On inspection, opening a stocked closed address consumes one token and adds one q bit and one cache bit, changing V by −4+2+1=−1. C closure removes a q bit and any cache bit. H retains q but clears its old latent cache on the next inspection. A broken-integrity cached latent bit is simply cleared. All other unchanged coordinates contribute zero. Thus any non-fixed inspection decreases V by at least one. Consequently the prepared recurrence reaches a full fixed point within V(X_initial) committed ticks. No physical energy or action is assigned to V or tokens.\n\n## 6. Exact close-branch duration and toggle balance\n\nLet delta=1 if any initial cached L bit lies on a broken T address, otherwise 0. For the active initial packet define D0=max(max_p(2r_p+q_p),delta). Then the exact number of committed C ticks is\n\nD_C=D0+(B−k)+2 sum_{j>k} max_p b_p^(j).\n\nProof: at one intact address, a prepared closed response with r tokens has r open/close pulse pairs, lasting 2r ticks. An initially open response first closes, giving 2r+1 ticks. Addresses advance simultaneously, so take the maximum. Broken-seat cached L clears in one response-null tick, explaining delta. The common quiescent point permits the next bank load; each remaining bank tuple costs one renewal tick and then exactly 2max b ticks. Zero tuples cost the pointer tick alone.\n\nThe total response opening count is S_initial. The closure count is S_initial+|q_initial|. C ends with all prepared stock spent, all slots visited and q=L_cache=0. These are exact conditional register-accounting identities, not physical support quantization, conservation of energy or a theorem of sustained external supply.\n\n## 7. Hold branch and projection boundary\n\nH never closes a previously open intact response. After at most one opening inspection and one cache-clearing inspection, a loaded nonzero packet latches. Hence committed H duration is at most (B−k)+2+delta; leading zero bank packets contribute pointer ticks. H can halt with active and unspent bank stock stranded. The C duration and exhaustion theorem do not apply to H.\n\nAn initially open H address with a previously viable latent cache can have unchanged q while omega changes from 1 to 0. Its viable index is +1; its idle correction is −1; the full budget is zero. Stopping on q or mu alone loses this source update.\n\nThe projection onto Theta alone is generally not autonomous even in this complete candidate. Same q=000, T=111 and L_cache=000 with r=000 versus r=100 produces different next responses. The complete state includes the missing stock/controller variables. This is a concrete finite illustration of E01/E03's source-fiber criterion; it does not identify those variables with native UD hidden state.\n\n## 8. Hodge bridge boundary\n\nOriginal C0926 §4.6 instead defines R_e^(HD)=c1,e²(c0,i²+c0,j²), R_p^(HD)=sum_{e in M_p}R_e^(HD), L_p^(HD)=1[R_p^(HD)>0]. Original hard integrity is T_int,e^hard=1[U_e†U_e=I] and pair T is its product (C0635 §9; C0926 §4.6).\n\nR^(RSP), integer stock, frozen Boolean T and the fixed identity frame have no proved identification with R^(HD), chain support, edge-transport dynamics or a native pre-event frame source. Copying T defines this candidate's integrity evolution; it does not derive physical integrity preservation, repair or breakage. RSP integer tokens are not energy, matter burden, Hodge amplitude, hbar or the retired universal scalar action. Its two-tick pulses are not the single-cell frequency 2 or a physical clock. C0621's instantaneous zero-rate limitation remains untouched.\n\n## 9. Verification, scope and next gate\n\nThe release contains reproducible constructor and parallel mathematical checks, a separate AI source/scope audit, paired traces, source snapshots and exact dependency declarations. Checks cover full-state stopping, cached-source nulls, balanced bit events, zero refills, stranded stock, admission and all S3 relabelings. Team AI checks do not constitute independent human review or CRL promotion. A generated trace is not target-hidden physical data or execution of the frozen sidecar.\n\nWhat is closed: the RSP-1 prepared finite programme is fully specified and its displayed finite properties have constructor checks and proofs.\n\nWhat remains OPEN: selecting a native response branch; proving a source map from Hodge/transport state to this counter carrier or replacing it with another typed native generator; endogenous repair/frame/renewal preparation; physical event clock; authenticated pre-event native data; independent adversarial review and a lawful scorer.\n\nRecommended next gate: test a declared HD-to-source realization or prove an obstruction on that named carrier before attributing any RSP prediction to UD. Priority: high. Preserve both branch results and their different stopping behavior. Physical promotion: 0.\n"
