    "content": "# Refinement histories and the missing detail-source law v0.1\n\n14 October 2026 · reading edition 0.14\n\nStatus: development — no registry entry. Exact conditional mathematics and scoped NO-GO results; constructor-team checks only. Native selection OPEN; independent human review PENDING; physical promotion 0. This adds a different-history test to RT01, not a correction of its same-sequence theorem.\n\n## 1. Explicit comparison contract\n\nThe common old carrier C0 is the full oriented simplex chain of a filled tetrahedron: dimensions (4,6,4,1), total15, boundary B0, old metric I. Compare its center-star history Cs, total29, and ordinary barycentric history Cb, total149. For each use a graded chain injection S and affine/exterior chain retraction R, with BS=SB0, RB=B0R, RS=I. Set Q=I−SR and declare\n\nH=RᵀR+QᵀQ, A=H⁻¹BᵀH−B.\n\nThis **conditional unit-detail calibration** is an authored premise, not a source-selected native metric. It preserves the complete old norm and generator: SᵀHS=I and AS=SA0, A0=B0ᵀ−B0. On kerR the pairing is Euclidean. These are direct-sum chain coordinates, not qubits or a tensor donor bank. Rates are compared in the same fixed internal time; rescaling rates or changing metrics is outside the contract.\n\n## 2. Star geometry and exact spectrum\n\nSource C0656 supplies a funded 1→4 center-star topology move. Our additional full graded interface fixes center vertex4 and uses four tetrahedra 0124,0134,0234,1234. S is identity on old degrees0–2 and sends 0123 to 0124−0134+0234−1234. R sends center4 to (e0+e1+e2+e3)/4 and extends by exterior powers. This choice is not inferred from NRF-1's inherited-edge inclusion and child charts.\n\nThe star f-vector is (5,10,10,4), with detail dimensions (1,4,6,3) and detail boundary ranks (1,3,3). The detail Laplacian is exactly5I on detail. The full skew characteristic polynomial is\n\nλ(λ²+4)^7(λ²+5)^7.\n\nThus star retains the old harmonic direction and seven coarse frequency2 pairs, and adds seven detail √5 pairs. All statements refer to the declared weighted generator, not the raw unit-metric star generator.\n\n## 3. Frequency capacity versus symmetry\n\nTheorem HC.1 — frequency capacity. Barycentric detail has squared-frequency5 eigenspace dimensions (2,7,8,3), giving ten √5 pairs. Boundary singular-pair multiplicities at √5 are (2,5,3), versus star (1,3,3). Therefore a 29→149 isometric full-generator embedding exists without symmetry constraints; a graded chain isometric embedding also exists. Choose the shared coarse code and compatible singular pairs in detail. Such encodings are nonunique and not source-selected, local or automatically S4-covariant.\n\nTheorem HC.2 — S4 obstruction. Average the 24 signed vertex-permutation actions to project onto the trivial representation. Exact intersections with squared-frequency5 have these graded dimensions:\n\n| History | Degree0 | Degree1 | Degree2 | Degree3 |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Center-star | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n| Barycentric | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n\nHence star has a trivial-representation √5 skew pair absent from the complete barycentric carrier: its coarse sector has only frequencies0 and2. Any S4-equivariant generator-intertwining isometry must preserve both frequency and the trivial representation, and cannot kill a nonzero vector. Therefore no such full star→barycentric embedding exists under this contract. The obstruction does not forbid non-equivariant encodings, another metric, another rate contract or augmented carriers.\n\n## 4. Coarse agreement is not full history equivalence\n\nTheorem HC.3 — lossy coarse comparison. T_b→s=Ss Rb agrees on all common coarse states, but kills all134 barycentric details. Its reverse T_s→b=Sb Rs kills all14 star details. Their compositions are coarse projectors, not identity. Moreover T_b→sᵀ Hs T_b→s=RbᵀRb, whereas Hb=RbᵀRb+QbᵀQb. Coarse observable pullbacks agree, but full fine-state norms and records are not retained. A full terminal bijection Cs↔Cb is imp