nds avoid the dense 286.75-GiB matrix. The nominal run encloses condition <706.570; the record-only verifier bounds the complete projection tail <1.132e-12. Four full-size noisy cases retain 1893 singular values above the frozen threshold with condition enclosures below 2029.\n- The temporal discovery gap theorem does not prove universal fitting convergence. Threshold count is not exact algebraic rank: a weak impulse fixture has rank at least 2203 while the retained count stays 1893. The codec recovers a finite recorded history, not hidden bulk state or a unique continuous-time generator.\n- Review intake remains HOLD: each supplied manifest mismatches all 12 existing target files; reviewer attribution/independence and original review-file bytes are absent. A different revision is possible. The audit preserves submissions and prior numerical certificates; no endorsement or intent is inferred.\n\n## Tracking and remaining returns\n\n| Item | Operational disposition | Remaining gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| [#176](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/issues/176) | Completed computational record; repository publication in review | Task completion only |\n| [#177](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/issues/177) | Blocked / review HOLD | Attributable, hash-bound corrected independent return |\n| [#178](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/issues/178) | Ready development work | Broader noisy fitting and declared failure domain |\n| [#136](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/issues/136) | Open | Native metric and observer selection |\n| [#144](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/issues/144) | Open | Joint acquisition/metrology, timing, dependence and costs |\n| [#130](https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/issues/130) | Open | Independent replay with pinned inputs and negative controls |\n\nProject: [Unified Dynamics](https://github.com/users/ud-tetra/projects/1/). No assignee, deadline, CRL advancement or independent review acceptance is inferred.\n\n## Coverage limits\n\nAll 26 accessible generated research pa