    "content": "# UD frozen new-seed phase campaign v0.1\n\nFour fresh bounded constructor records certify unique matching to the pinned\nfitted reference. A fifth, deliberately oversized impulse yields a retained\nmodel/order HOLD. Physical promotion 0; development — no registry entry;\nindependent review pending.\n\n| New record | Learned temporal order (floating discovery) | Phase certificate, radians/sample |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| dense_216104 | 105 | <0.000500262 |\n| dense_216105 | 105 | <0.000499343 |\n| dense_216106 | 105 | <0.000502489 |\n| block_512_216107 | 105 | <0.000496848 |\n| oversized_impulse_216108 | 106 | Proposer model/order HOLD |\n\nBounds are a posteriori errors relative to the fixed learned reference, not\nobserved parameter errors or physical-frequency measurements. The block-sign\ncase holds each error sign for512 consecutive samples. Three new dense seeds\nand this dependence pattern all meet both declared additive gates. Every bounded\n62-vector uses exactly31/32 of the squared vector-error budget. The oversized\nimpulse intentionally violates both gates. Its even learned order106 is outside\nthe proposer's stationary-plus-conjugate-pairs model. That HOLD is not a claim\nthat the record's true full-Hankel signature fails.\n\n## Frozen execution and checks\n\nCAMPAIGN_FREEZE.json binds all recipe seeds, code and input hashes before noise\ngeneration. DATA_FREEZE.json binds all five complete raw records and exact error\nchecks before fitting. No seed, threshold, reference, estimator or mathematical\nproof was adjusted after these outcomes. Four successful original proposals are\nbyte-identical to the instrumented ones; the fifth pair has equal HOLD receipts.\nTen fresh original/instrumented executions were performed.\n\nAll93,950,770 actual additive scalar differences were checked against the\nlosslessly restored baseline. Four saved-array phase residual replays agree;\n13 tests pass, including scalar/vector boundary distinctions and large-integer\nsquared-norm overflow protection. All five raw records were separately\nregenerated with identical hashes and gate results. This is same-constructor\ndeterministic reproduction, not independent review or blinded execution.\n\nThe PR189 proof helpers and original/instrumented proposer code retain their\npublished bytes (SOURCE_IDENTITY.json). Only the adapter's record/report/witness\nlineage changes; patches are included. Exact residual formulas, fixed phases,\nframe-constant recomputation, angle rounding and strict matching gates are\nunchanged. THEOREMS.md reproduces the direct-span argument; EXACT_GATES.md proves\nthe encoded additive gates and states the scope.\n\n## Portable phase replay\n\nExtract the core ZIP and all four WITNESS archives listed in WITNESS_INDEX.json\ninto one directory. Each witness archive contains its actual floating arrays\nand the corresponding original proposal needed for byte comparison. Then run:\n\n```\nOPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 python replay_package.py\n```\n\nPython3.12, NumPy2.3.5, SciPy1.17.0, python-flint0.9.0 are the recorded runtime.\nThis verifies package hashes and recomputes all four available actual-array\nphase certificates in a temporary copy. It checks the oversized HOLD/audit\nreceipts but does not rerun its proposer. Every float array, auxiliary reduction,\nactual proposal and original proposal required by this replay is retained.\n\n## Optional full raw-record regeneration\n\nRaw records and the parent lossless codec are omitted to avoid duplicating\nlarge source evidence. Obtain the UD repository with the canonical codec path\nand exact hashes specified by CAMPAIGN_FREEZE.json. From the extracted package:\n\n```\nOPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 python reproduce_records.py --repo /path/to/UD --destination /new/empty/path\n```\n\nThis restores the baseline from the hash-checked parent codec, regenerates all\nfive raw records, rechecks every additive coordinate, and compares all resulting\nrecord hashes/gate receipts with DATA_FREEZE.json. The destination must not\nexist. The normal portable phase replay does not silently claim this source\nreconstruction. RAW_REGENERATION_RECEIPT.json records the separate execution\nperformed for this campaign.\n\n## Remaining scope\n\nThis is five synthetic fixtures on one known baseline; four certified phase\nruns do not establish stochastic coverage, uniform whole2^-20-ball phase\nmatching, arbitrary excitation loss or global fitter convergence. Floating\ncomponent discovery is distinct from exact algebraic rank and the full1893-value\nHankel criterion. No new full-Hankel verification or dense Hankel allocation is\nclaimed. No timing/preparation/SI calibration, acquisition/metrology admission,\nindependent source custody, independent review, hidden-state recovery or physical\nidentification is inferred. The nominal747-dimensional observer kernel and the\nseparation of62 history channels from189 diagnostic outputs remain unchanged.\nTask178 and review HOLD177 remain open. O03 tolerances remain protocol controls.\n"
