    "content": "# Historical runner coverage and source-selected W audit v0.1\n\nDevelopment — no registry entry. EXACT FINITE OPERATOR CHECKS plus a separately labeled NUMERICAL CSV diagnostic. Constructor audit; physical promotion0.\n\n## Result and scope amendment\n\nThe historical runners verify supplied carrier identities. They do not construct W from native incidence data or verify membership in the selected Pachner sector. Nevertheless,the missing finite construction is available in the recovered selector,Darboux-map and30-by6 CSV sources. This audit independently rebuilds its finite operator identities from oriented simplicial incidence,without executing any archived program.\n\nEarlier statements that native-W admission was broadly open are scope-amended: an explicit finite W is now source-recovered and its source construction is checked under the declared unit metric,S4 averaging,complex-compatible projection and lower-response selection convention. An autonomous physical/source law choosing that convention,event-state identification and physical correspondence are not closed.\n\n## Exact finite reconstruction\n\nOn U=boundary(Delta4),use all ascending simplices of sizes1–4,total dimension30. Assemble integer skew A with the stated oriented boundaries. Embed K_minus={0123,0124} and K_plus={0134,0234,1234};form D=-A_plus^2+A_minus^2. Average D over the24 oriented S4 actions fixing vertex4. The exact character projector P_std has rank12. Set R=P_std Dbar P_std and\n\nC=(R+A^T R A/5)/2.\n\nThe fresh rational calculation verifies\n\nC^2-(23/8)C+(129/160)P_std=0,\n\n[C,A]=0.\n\nIts two standard-sector roots are (115 plus/minus sqrt(8065))/80. Their gap is sqrt(8065)/40>0;the lower spectral projector is\n\nP_evt=(1/2)P_std+sqrt(8065)*( (115/2)P_std-40C )/8065.\n\nCalculating in Q(sqrt(8065)) as rational coefficient pairs gives exact idempotence,trace/rank6,A/S4 commutation and A^2 P_evt=-5 P_evt. The lower-root selection is the declared source rule;the algebra identifies both eigensectors and does not independently derive a dynamical preference for the lower one.\n\nLet P0 be the rank3 vertex-standard projector on vertices0,1,2,3. Exact checks give\n\nP0 P_evt P0=alpha P0,\nalpha=(1+89/sqrt(8065))/2,\nP0 P_evt A P_evt P0=0.\n\nThus with the source's explicit orthonormal standard frame U0,define Q=alpha^(-1/2)P_evt U0 and P=AQ/sqrt5. These equalities imply Q^TQ=P^TP=I3 and Q^TP=0. Therefore W=(Q P) is an orthonormal30-by6 frame of the selected sector. With J=A/sqrt5,the induced convention is J0=[[0,-I],[I,0]] and W^T J W=J0. Consequently W^T A W=sqrt5 J0. This is a finite internal Hodge construction,not a physical clock identification.\n\nThe recovered exact-expression CSV is additionally compared componentwise with this reconstruction at100-decimal precision. The residual is reported as a numerical diagnostic,not a certified interval or exact symbolic comparison of every printed radical expression. The exact finite construction above does not rely on rounded CSV columns.\n\n## Historical coverage\n\n| Gate | CRL2c runner | CRL2d runner |\n|---|---|---|\n| Supplied W orthonormality,T=W^T,Theta=WRW^T | Checked | Checked |\n| Basic parity intertwining,event anti-symplecticity,copy-swap sign | Checked | Checked |\n| I_c commutes with parity | Checked | Checked |\n| Full reciprocal diagonal family I_c=diag(cI,c^-1I) | Not enforced | Definition check added |\n| Explicit c>0 guard | Not enforced | Not explicitly enforced |\n| Native A,selected P_evt or source-derived W | Not checked | Not checked |\n| Repaired typed full composite including W | Not checked | Not checked |\n\nThe first runner's infnorm is maximum absolute entry;the second uses maximum absolute row sum. Their1e-10 tolerance is a protocol control,not a theory constant or a common norm certificate. The coverage audit parses their source text/AST only;neither archived runner is executed.\n\nFresh exact fixtures show an arbitrary orthonormal coordinate W can satisfy these parity residuals while failing A^2 W=-5W. Likewise diag(2I3,3I3) commutes with parity but is not the reciprocal family;the added replication-definition check rejects that example. These are coverage distinctions,not evidence that historical scored cases were invalid or that the underlying parity identities are false. No historical PASS is silently replaced.\n\n## Remaining premises and reuse\n\nThe actual W's finite source construction is now checked. The lower-response choice,unit-weight source scope,source-selected preparation,event response-to-state identification,SA023,physical time/parity,and independent review remain separate gates. Parity on the Hodge complement is still not selected. Historical custody/replication provenance gaps remain open.\n\nA future expanded test contract should freeze native A/P_evt checks,typed-composite checks,positive-c eligibility and a declared norm before generating fresh blind cases. Such a contract would be new;these checks are not retroactively inserted into the old runners. Issue126 remains open for broader proof/source coverage. No new registry/CRL promotion. Physical promotion0.\n\nMissing Gap2_FINAL_Finite_Genesis.png remains unavailable and unused;re-upload for image-dependent work.\n"
